1
00:00:03,353 --> 00:00:06,040
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

2
00:00:15,524 --> 00:00:17,894
(The trotters are perfectly boiled by now.)

3
00:00:18,671 --> 00:00:20,071
(The first round of boiling is complete.)

4
00:00:20,071 --> 00:00:21,501
(She's about to take the trotters out of the water.)

5
00:00:22,001 --> 00:00:24,811
(Pulled out through clouds of hot steam)

6
00:00:26,011 --> 00:00:28,481
(It's plump and bouncy.)

7
00:00:29,583 --> 00:00:30,583
Gosh, it's hot.

8
00:00:31,253 --> 00:00:32,753
(Once the trotters are out of the water,)

9
00:00:32,753 --> 00:00:34,193
(it'll be boiled again with aromatic spices.)

10
00:00:34,393 --> 00:00:35,753
I need to throw it away.

11
00:00:35,753 --> 00:00:36,923
(Jung Ah is about to wash the pot...)

12
00:00:36,923 --> 00:00:38,123
(for the second round of boiling.)

13
00:00:38,223 --> 00:00:39,333
Isn't it too heavy?

14
00:00:40,193 --> 00:00:41,263
(Lifting easily)

15
00:00:41,263 --> 00:00:42,363
- Move out of the way.
- Will you throw it away here?

16
00:00:42,363 --> 00:00:43,433
Move out of the way.

17
00:00:45,403 --> 00:00:47,703
(What is that sound?)

18
00:00:47,973 --> 00:00:49,133
- What's the matter?
- What is it?

19
00:00:49,133 --> 00:00:50,243
What's wrong, Sun Young?

20
00:00:51,343 --> 00:00:53,843
Oh, no. There's a snake!

21
00:00:54,073 --> 00:00:56,583
(A snake?)

22
00:00:57,483 --> 00:00:59,683
- Where is it?
- My goodness.

23
00:00:59,683 --> 00:01:00,883
There's a snake.

24
00:01:01,183 --> 00:01:02,583
Why are you going in there?

25
00:01:02,583 --> 00:01:03,623
(The production crew is also startled by news of a snake.)

26
00:01:03,883 --> 00:01:05,053
(Murmuring)

27
00:01:05,053 --> 00:01:06,123
My goodness.

28
00:01:06,493 --> 00:01:07,653
- Where is the snake?
- There's a snake.

29
00:01:07,653 --> 00:01:09,263
Where is it?

30
00:01:09,263 --> 00:01:10,293
(Where's the snake?)

31
00:01:10,423 --> 00:01:11,963
Why are you going in there?

32
00:01:12,293 --> 00:01:14,193
Where is it?

33
00:01:14,533 --> 00:01:16,503
- It's dangerous. Don't go in.
- Don't go.

34
00:01:16,733 --> 00:01:17,933
- Hey.
- You Seok.

35
00:01:17,933 --> 00:01:19,233
Don't go there, You Seok.

36
00:01:19,373 --> 00:01:20,773
What is he doing?

37
00:01:21,103 --> 00:01:22,603
My goodness. You Seok.

38
00:01:22,703 --> 00:01:24,473
You Seok, come back here.

39
00:01:24,473 --> 00:01:25,473
You can't use that.

40
00:01:25,473 --> 00:01:27,143
No way. What are you doing?

41
00:01:27,173 --> 00:01:28,243
- Gosh.
- Oh, my.

42
00:01:29,383 --> 00:01:30,413
What happened?

43
00:01:32,513 --> 00:01:34,853
(Serious)

44
00:01:35,153 --> 00:01:36,583
Guys, go and take a look.

45
00:01:37,023 --> 00:01:38,683
He's going in to catch it.

46
00:01:38,783 --> 00:01:39,793
But...

47
00:01:39,793 --> 00:01:41,423
(Serious)

48
00:01:42,099 --> 00:01:43,823
(Screaming)

49
00:01:44,423 --> 00:01:46,393
(Everyone is extremely tense.)

50
00:01:46,833 --> 00:01:49,763
Don't go in there, You Seok!

51
00:01:50,063 --> 00:01:51,533
Are you out of your mind?

52
00:01:51,863 --> 00:01:52,903
Goodness.

53
00:01:54,173 --> 00:01:55,973
(Did he catch the snake with his hand?)

54
00:01:56,873 --> 00:01:58,703
(And he runs outside.)

55
00:01:58,703 --> 00:01:59,713
It's a snake.

56
00:02:00,913 --> 00:02:01,943
It's a snake.

57
00:02:02,413 --> 00:02:03,543
It's a snake.

58
00:02:06,053 --> 00:02:08,483
(The snake remains completely still.)

59
00:02:08,713 --> 00:02:10,253
Are you out of your mind?

60
00:02:10,253 --> 00:02:11,253
It's a snake.

61
00:02:11,253 --> 00:02:12,483
(Laughing)

62
00:02:13,253 --> 00:02:15,153
- My goodness.
- You startled me.

63
00:02:15,293 --> 00:02:16,463
You really startled me.

64
00:02:17,563 --> 00:02:20,033
(Actually, it was just a toy snake.)

65
00:02:20,333 --> 00:02:21,963
(Laughing)

66
00:02:22,633 --> 00:02:24,133
(The four siblings' prank...)

67
00:02:24,133 --> 00:02:25,973
(on the production crew was a huge success.)

68
00:02:26,333 --> 00:02:27,703
I did all that just for this.

69
00:02:28,503 --> 00:02:30,973
(Her talent put to excess use)

70
00:02:30,973 --> 00:02:31,973
Sae Hee.

71
00:02:31,973 --> 00:02:33,743
(Terrified even while knowing that it's fake)

72
00:02:33,943 --> 00:02:36,383
I went all out while running around barefoot.

73
00:02:37,213 --> 00:02:38,413
(On the cement floor)

74
00:02:38,413 --> 00:02:40,083
(Even over the gravel)

75
00:02:40,483 --> 00:02:41,813
(Sun Young, the barefoot actress...)

76
00:02:41,813 --> 00:02:43,053
(ran around without shoes to give it her all.)

77
00:02:43,197 --> 00:02:45,627
Sun Young is such an amazing actress.

78
00:02:46,037 --> 00:02:47,537
My feet are killing me.

79
00:02:47,537 --> 00:02:49,907
I know. She went through it barefoot.

80
00:02:49,907 --> 00:02:52,207
(Sun Young's barefoot dedication stole the show.)

81
00:02:52,437 --> 00:02:54,037
- Did you bring it from Seoul?
- Of course.

82
00:02:54,677 --> 00:02:55,777
We came up with this...

83
00:02:56,377 --> 00:02:59,077
the moment we got taken away on the boat.

84
00:02:59,947 --> 00:03:01,117
We couldn't be the only ones getting pranked.

85
00:03:01,977 --> 00:03:03,847
We planned this for a month.

86
00:03:04,217 --> 00:03:06,617
(A month ago)

87
00:03:06,917 --> 00:03:09,117
(Why?)

88
00:03:09,427 --> 00:03:11,887
(What's going on here?)

89
00:03:12,157 --> 00:03:13,597
(What's going on?)

90
00:03:13,927 --> 00:03:15,757
(A mental breakdown)

91
00:03:16,897 --> 00:03:19,667
(The humiliating kidnapping they endured on the first day)

92
00:03:20,397 --> 00:03:22,597
(You Seok, someday...)

93
00:03:22,767 --> 00:03:24,667
(we have to get our revenge.)

94
00:03:25,007 --> 00:03:26,807
(We definitely have to get them back.)

95
00:03:27,037 --> 00:03:28,377
(And so began the siblings' secret scheme.)

96
00:03:28,377 --> 00:03:29,877
(How will we fool the production staff?)

97
00:03:29,877 --> 00:03:31,207
(Then the toy snake idea came up.)

98
00:03:31,207 --> 00:03:33,017
(Shall I buy a toy snake?)

99
00:03:33,017 --> 00:03:36,217
(The snake idea was chosen with enthusiastic approval.)

100
00:03:36,587 --> 00:03:37,617
How about this?

101
00:03:37,617 --> 00:03:38,617
(A few days earlier, somewhere in Seoul)

102
00:03:38,617 --> 00:03:39,957
What's our final move?

103
00:03:39,957 --> 00:03:41,157
Throwing the snake?

104
00:03:41,157 --> 00:03:42,987
Because he got so sweaty,

105
00:03:42,987 --> 00:03:44,557
he goes inside to change his shirt.

106
00:03:44,557 --> 00:03:46,097
Then he leaves the snake there.

107
00:03:46,227 --> 00:03:48,557
(Before making dinner)

108
00:03:48,857 --> 00:03:50,567
(Rummaging around)

109
00:03:50,797 --> 00:03:52,327
(You Seok secretly took out the toy snake...)

110
00:03:52,327 --> 00:03:53,897
(that he brought in advance.)

111
00:03:54,497 --> 00:03:57,067
(Walking casually)

112
00:03:57,407 --> 00:03:59,007
(I am...)

113
00:03:59,007 --> 00:04:00,307
(going in now.)

114
00:04:01,077 --> 00:04:04,247
(Got it)

115
00:04:05,147 --> 00:04:06,377
I'm going to the bathroom.

116
00:04:08,347 --> 00:04:10,917
(Coming back out with empty hands)

117
00:04:11,247 --> 00:04:13,457
I'm going to use the bathroom.

118
00:04:13,457 --> 00:04:14,487
Okay.

119
00:04:15,517 --> 00:04:18,387
Jung Ah, I'll go and use the bathroom.

120
00:04:18,387 --> 00:04:19,387
Of course.

121
00:04:19,387 --> 00:04:22,427
(Unable to hide his excitement at the signal to begin)

122
00:04:23,297 --> 00:04:24,467
(Screaming)

123
00:04:24,467 --> 00:04:26,867
(Led by Sun Young,)

124
00:04:27,467 --> 00:04:30,667
(the four siblings began their acting tour de force.)

125
00:04:31,237 --> 00:04:33,937
(Sending the production staff into complete panic)

126
00:04:34,337 --> 00:04:37,577
(The production staff fell for it completely.)

127
00:04:38,577 --> 00:04:40,377
When I went inside to catch the snake,

128
00:04:40,377 --> 00:04:41,847
I expected someone to follow me.

129
00:04:42,347 --> 00:04:44,417
- No one went after him.
- No one.

130
00:04:44,987 --> 00:04:46,317
I went to catch the snake.

131
00:04:46,987 --> 00:04:49,857
We expected the staff to come inside.

132
00:04:50,587 --> 00:04:53,557
(I was on my way over with a shovel.)

133
00:04:55,097 --> 00:04:57,897
I got so caught up in the moment that I strained my neck.

134
00:04:59,637 --> 00:05:01,437
(The production staff says, "We won't forget.")

135
00:05:01,437 --> 00:05:04,007
You Seok kept laughing inside because no one could see him.

136
00:05:04,807 --> 00:05:06,937
- We're done cooking.
- Right.

137
00:05:06,937 --> 00:05:08,637
- Jung Ah has to make trotters.
- Yes.

138
00:05:09,077 --> 00:05:11,877
Today, I'm determined to make trotters with zero unpleasant smell.

139
00:05:12,207 --> 00:05:14,047
(Mission: Make trotters without the smell)

140
00:05:14,647 --> 00:05:17,487
(What's Chef Yum's secret to getting rid of that pork smell?)

141
00:05:18,087 --> 00:05:20,317
(Scrubbing)

142
00:05:20,617 --> 00:05:23,287
(Rinsing the boiled trotters)

143
00:05:23,287 --> 00:05:24,657
(If you rinse the trotters after the first boil, you can remove...)

144
00:05:24,657 --> 00:05:26,057
(the impurities that cause the unpleasant smell...)

145
00:05:26,057 --> 00:05:27,357
(and give it a cleaner flavour.)

146
00:05:27,757 --> 00:05:30,567
(I won't miss even the tiniest bit of impurities.)

147
00:05:31,127 --> 00:05:33,837
(Once the trotters are thoroughly cleaned,)

148
00:05:34,167 --> 00:05:36,407
(add soy sauce to the boiling water.)

149
00:05:37,137 --> 00:05:39,437
(Then add dark soy sauce to deepen the colour.)

150
00:05:39,937 --> 00:05:42,537
(Making a base to bring out the colour and flavour of trotters)

151
00:05:43,307 --> 00:05:45,847
(Adding trotters)

152
00:05:46,347 --> 00:05:47,677
(Two pieces)

153
00:05:48,077 --> 00:05:49,617
(Three pieces)

154
00:05:50,217 --> 00:05:52,787
(trotters keeps going in generously.)

155
00:05:54,387 --> 00:05:57,727
(It's finally over after eight pieces.)

156
00:05:57,987 --> 00:05:59,657
We have to add two eggs.

157
00:05:59,657 --> 00:06:01,197
(Shall I get rid of the porky smell again?)

158
00:06:01,197 --> 00:06:02,197
Eggs?

159
00:06:02,397 --> 00:06:04,327
(Secret 1 for removing the smell: Soju)

160
00:06:04,527 --> 00:06:05,597
I have to get rid of the smell.

161
00:06:06,667 --> 00:06:08,697
Getting rid of the smell is the most important.

162
00:06:08,697 --> 00:06:09,737
(Bad smell, go away!)

163
00:06:09,867 --> 00:06:12,537
(Secret 2 for removing the smell: Bay leaves)

164
00:06:12,837 --> 00:06:15,277
(Dried chilli peppers, green onions, pears, onions)

165
00:06:15,877 --> 00:06:18,547
(Secret 3 for removing the smell: Adding various ingredients)

166
00:06:19,107 --> 00:06:21,247
(Cinnamon sticks are good for getting rid of unwanted odours.)

167
00:06:22,117 --> 00:06:24,347
(Whole garlic cloves peeled by Sun Young)

168
00:06:25,217 --> 00:06:27,417
(We can't forget the whole black peppercorns.)

169
00:06:28,187 --> 00:06:30,727
(Adding doenjang from a container)

170
00:06:31,187 --> 00:06:32,287
Let's see. Did I add everything?

171
00:06:33,827 --> 00:06:35,657
I'll add some sugar.

172
00:06:36,527 --> 00:06:38,927
(Adding sugar to tenderize the meat and finish it)

173
00:06:39,997 --> 00:06:41,167
(All you have to do is let the trotters simmer away.)

174
00:06:41,167 --> 00:06:43,867
Let it boil nice and hard.

175
00:06:44,367 --> 00:06:47,137
I added all kinds of things to get rid of the smell.

176
00:06:48,137 --> 00:06:50,907
(You Seok who is in charge of seasoned dried radish)

177
00:06:51,807 --> 00:06:52,877
You Seok, what are you making?

178
00:06:53,547 --> 00:06:55,117
- Seasoned dried radish?
- After seasoning dried radish...

179
00:06:55,117 --> 00:06:56,217
What's this?

180
00:06:56,617 --> 00:06:57,617
Dried chilli pepper leaves.

181
00:06:58,087 --> 00:06:59,757
- For seasoned dried radish?
- Yes.

182
00:07:00,757 --> 00:07:01,757
These are good with dried radish.

183
00:07:01,757 --> 00:07:02,957
(You Seok confidently pulls out the dried chilli pepper leaves.)

184
00:07:03,487 --> 00:07:04,527
Have you made it before?

185
00:07:05,587 --> 00:07:07,897
- You just try everything.
- So you haven't.

186
00:07:07,897 --> 00:07:08,997
(Laughing)

187
00:07:09,427 --> 00:07:11,227
There's a first time for everything.

188
00:07:11,227 --> 00:07:12,267
(It's his first time making seasoned dried radish.)

189
00:07:12,267 --> 00:07:13,897
You learn by doing.

190
00:07:13,897 --> 00:07:14,897
(It's not that complicated. You just wing it.)

191
00:07:15,537 --> 00:07:18,207
(Tossing dried chilli pepper leaves into the boiling water)

192
00:07:18,607 --> 00:07:19,807
Thirty seconds.

193
00:07:20,077 --> 00:07:21,637
One, two...

194
00:07:22,037 --> 00:07:24,147
I'll make the seasoning for the dried radish.

195
00:07:24,877 --> 00:07:25,907
You just do it by feel.

196
00:07:27,217 --> 00:07:29,617
You throw in this and that to make it.

197
00:07:30,917 --> 00:07:34,057
(Sprinkling in chilli powder)

198
00:07:34,517 --> 00:07:37,487
Where's the thick soy sauce? Is the yangjo soy sauce better?

199
00:07:37,487 --> 00:07:38,587
Where's the yangjo soy sauce?

200
00:07:39,357 --> 00:07:40,457
Should I just add thick soy sauce?

201
00:07:41,727 --> 00:07:42,727
Should I add yangjo soy sauce?

202
00:07:42,727 --> 00:07:43,767
(I don't know anything about recipes.)

203
00:07:43,767 --> 00:07:44,827
Should I add thick soy sauce?

204
00:07:45,867 --> 00:07:48,937
(Casually pouring in thick soy sauce)

205
00:07:49,337 --> 00:07:52,067
(Tuna fish sauce, sand lance sauce, oligosaccharide)

206
00:07:52,637 --> 00:07:54,907
(Also adding garlic and sugar)

207
00:07:55,577 --> 00:07:58,777
(And ginger juice to remove odours and add a rich flavour)

208
00:07:59,507 --> 00:08:02,177
(He makes the seasoning on the spot without hesitation.)

209
00:08:02,877 --> 00:08:05,317
(Don't I do it well without recipes?)

210
00:08:05,787 --> 00:08:06,787
- Jung Ah.
- Yes?

211
00:08:06,787 --> 00:08:07,857
Can you taste it?

212
00:08:08,157 --> 00:08:10,057
- What is it?
- Seasoning for the dried radish.

213
00:08:10,057 --> 00:08:11,057
Dried radish?

214
00:08:11,057 --> 00:08:13,227
(Asking Chef Yum for confirmation now that he's made it)

215
00:08:13,457 --> 00:08:15,897
(Analysing the taste)

216
00:08:16,327 --> 00:08:17,967
It's good, but it's a little too salty.

217
00:08:18,167 --> 00:08:20,137
- Is it? But I have to mix them.
- Of course.

218
00:08:20,397 --> 00:08:22,597
Don't add all the seasoning. Add it as you go.

219
00:08:24,507 --> 00:08:28,107
(Squeeze the dried radish that has been soaking in cooking wine)

220
00:08:28,537 --> 00:08:31,177
(Rinse the boiled dried chilli pepper leaves)

221
00:08:31,747 --> 00:08:35,517
(Bring the dried radish and dried chilli pepper leaves together)

222
00:08:35,977 --> 00:08:37,387
(Adding the seasoning)

223
00:08:37,987 --> 00:08:41,717
(All he has to do is mix them up.)

224
00:08:42,317 --> 00:08:45,127
(Massaging gently)

225
00:08:45,657 --> 00:08:49,057
(The dried radish is dressed in a beautiful red sauce.)

226
00:08:49,727 --> 00:08:51,767
Gosh, that looks good. You should add sesame seeds...

227
00:08:52,227 --> 00:08:53,867
- Do you want to try it?
- and sesame oil.

228
00:08:54,467 --> 00:08:56,707
- Did you already add sesame oil?
- No, not yet.

229
00:08:56,907 --> 00:08:58,907
(Try it first.)

230
00:08:59,207 --> 00:09:02,237
(Analysing the taste)

231
00:09:02,437 --> 00:09:03,477
It's good.

232
00:09:03,477 --> 00:09:05,147
- Is it not too bland?
- No.

233
00:09:05,147 --> 00:09:06,847
You need to add sesame oil and sesame seeds.

234
00:09:07,777 --> 00:09:08,947
I'll pour some sesame oil for you.

235
00:09:08,947 --> 00:09:09,947
(Under the supervisor's direction)

236
00:09:09,947 --> 00:09:11,417
Please pour it in.

237
00:09:11,417 --> 00:09:13,517
(Adding sesame oil and sesame seeds)

238
00:09:13,987 --> 00:09:16,787
(Massaging it gently one more time)

239
00:09:17,627 --> 00:09:20,257
(Taking a bite to taste)

240
00:09:20,897 --> 00:09:23,897
(One more bite to see if it tastes good)

241
00:09:24,997 --> 00:09:26,367
You Seok, did you make it?

242
00:09:26,367 --> 00:09:27,697
(You Seok's first seasoned dried radish is ready.)

243
00:09:28,067 --> 00:09:29,067
When did he make it so fast?

244
00:09:29,297 --> 00:09:32,307
(Sun Young tastes it too.)

245
00:09:32,767 --> 00:09:34,237
You Seok, it's delicious.

246
00:09:34,607 --> 00:09:35,677
Does it taste okay?

247
00:09:35,807 --> 00:09:37,047
(Glancing?)

248
00:09:37,047 --> 00:09:38,047
Can you make it sweeter?

249
00:09:38,477 --> 00:09:40,747
- Shall I add some sugar?
- Right?

250
00:09:40,747 --> 00:09:42,377
- You can make it a little sweeter.
- I can add sugar...

251
00:09:42,377 --> 00:09:44,287
- Otherwise, it tastes good.
- or oligosaccharide.

252
00:09:44,287 --> 00:09:45,817
Really? Make it sweeter?

253
00:09:45,817 --> 00:09:48,587
(The mild flavour lover)

254
00:09:49,617 --> 00:09:52,087
(Intimidated)

255
00:09:52,287 --> 00:09:54,297
- Did you see her eyes just now?
- To your taste...

256
00:09:54,297 --> 00:09:56,197
- Did you see her eyes just now?
- I did.

257
00:09:56,197 --> 00:09:57,227
(Actually, I saw them.)

258
00:09:57,327 --> 00:10:00,137
This is enough, Jung Ah. The sweetness is perfect like this.

259
00:10:00,367 --> 00:10:02,497
(She intimidates her with a single look.)

260
00:10:03,037 --> 00:10:04,267
Should I chop the garlic scapes?

261
00:10:05,237 --> 00:10:07,777
- Cut them the way you know.
- Okay.

262
00:10:08,307 --> 00:10:10,807
Take them with you. I'm done with them.

263
00:10:11,777 --> 00:10:12,807
