520
00:20:42,537 --> 00:20:45,707
(And pickled onions You Seok made back in Seoul)

521
00:20:45,907 --> 00:20:48,847
How does Jung Ah cook everything so well?

522
00:20:48,847 --> 00:20:50,277
(A generous trotters feast is finally spread across the table.)

523
00:20:50,277 --> 00:20:51,787
All right, let's eat now.

524
00:20:51,787 --> 00:20:54,117
- Let's eat.
- Let's eat.

525
00:20:55,417 --> 00:20:57,787
Okay. Mix them in there.

526
00:20:58,987 --> 00:21:02,057
(The makguksu goes into a large mixing bowl.)

527
00:21:03,357 --> 00:21:04,527
Gosh, I'm hungry.

528
00:21:04,667 --> 00:21:06,027
Should we serve on individual plates?

529
00:21:06,867 --> 00:21:12,067
(The makguksu chef gives it a hands-on mixing service.)

530
00:21:13,337 --> 00:21:14,477
(The noodles are tossed in a sweet and tangy red sauce.)

531
00:21:14,477 --> 00:21:16,277
I can tell from the smell that it's delicious.

532
00:21:16,277 --> 00:21:17,347
(The noodles are tossed in a sweet and tangy red sauce.)

533
00:21:17,407 --> 00:21:19,247
It's made by Yoon Seo.

534
00:21:19,247 --> 00:21:20,247
(A volunteer taste tester appears.)

535
00:21:20,247 --> 00:21:21,717
How will her makguksu taste?

536
00:21:22,147 --> 00:21:23,317
(It's time for the taste test, and the tension kicks in.)

537
00:21:23,317 --> 00:21:24,317
I'm so scared.

538
00:21:26,087 --> 00:21:29,157
(The nerve-racking moment of the first bite)

539
00:21:29,917 --> 00:21:30,987
It's good.

540
00:21:31,627 --> 00:21:33,997
- Yoon Seo, it's delicious.
- Is it?

541
00:21:34,897 --> 00:21:35,957
Yoon Seo.

542
00:21:35,957 --> 00:21:38,667
(You Seok gives garlic trotters to Yoon Seo.)

543
00:21:40,697 --> 00:21:42,637
(Humming)

544
00:21:43,697 --> 00:21:44,767
Seriously...

545
00:21:45,207 --> 00:21:46,237
(You Seok also tries some garlic trotters.)

546
00:21:46,737 --> 00:21:48,377
(One bite in, and the exclamations begin.)

547
00:21:49,037 --> 00:21:50,107
The trotters are incredible.

548
00:21:50,107 --> 00:21:51,277
(Over the perfectly cooked, chewy and bouncy trotters)

549
00:21:51,277 --> 00:21:52,347
I'm not kidding.

550
00:21:52,977 --> 00:21:55,177
The garlic sauce has a nice kick to it.

551
00:21:55,177 --> 00:21:56,517
(The spicy garlic sauce cuts right through the richness.)

552
00:21:57,247 --> 00:22:01,457
(Jung Ah piles on a generous amount of garlic sauce.)

553
00:22:01,757 --> 00:22:02,857
- It has a kick to it.
- Yes.

554
00:22:03,057 --> 00:22:04,527
Seosan is reclaimed farmland,

555
00:22:04,927 --> 00:22:07,797
so the garlic grows...

556
00:22:07,797 --> 00:22:08,797
(The honorary ambassador of Seosan garlic appears suddenly.)

557
00:22:08,797 --> 00:22:09,827
It grows really well there.

558
00:22:10,797 --> 00:22:11,927
It's even better than takeout.

559
00:22:11,927 --> 00:22:12,927
(Seasonal garlic makes the trotters even more delicious.)

560
00:22:13,127 --> 00:22:15,297
It's ready now.

561
00:22:15,837 --> 00:22:17,767
You're supposed to wrap trotters with makguksu, right?

562
00:22:18,207 --> 00:22:20,937
trotters is always served with tray noodles.

563
00:22:20,937 --> 00:22:21,977
(Trotters and makguksu make the perfect match.)

564
00:22:22,537 --> 00:22:26,177
(Just like this)

565
00:22:26,707 --> 00:22:29,547
(Delicious plus delicious equals more delicious.)

566
00:22:29,977 --> 00:22:31,987
(Jung Ah takes a bite of trotters first.)

567
00:22:32,617 --> 00:22:35,917
(She cleanses the palate with spicy makguksu.)

568
00:22:36,717 --> 00:22:39,457
(Slurping in)

569
00:22:40,127 --> 00:22:42,657
(The spicy, tangy sauce cuts through the richness of trotters.)

570
00:22:43,297 --> 00:22:45,867
(You Seok piles up vegetables on the noodles.)

571
00:22:46,397 --> 00:22:49,467
(Crunch)

572
00:22:50,297 --> 00:22:53,607
(The vegetables leave the mouth feeling fresh and light.)

573
00:22:54,537 --> 00:22:59,147
(The makguksu chef also takes a bite.)

574
00:22:59,577 --> 00:23:01,147
The sauce tasted salty on its own,

575
00:23:01,147 --> 00:23:02,717
but it works perfectly when everything is mixed.

576
00:23:02,817 --> 00:23:03,817
It's good.

577
00:23:04,317 --> 00:23:06,047
- You can make it now, right?
- Yes.

578
00:23:06,047 --> 00:23:07,317
- You can make it.
- I can make it tastier.

579
00:23:07,317 --> 00:23:09,087
It'd be good even if it were spicier.

580
00:23:09,857 --> 00:23:11,987
(It's the best.)

581
00:23:13,127 --> 00:23:14,997
(After a bite of chewy trotters)

582
00:23:16,257 --> 00:23:19,927
(She tries it with You Seok's dried radish this time.)

583
00:23:20,067 --> 00:23:21,367
Dried radish is good too.

584
00:23:21,367 --> 00:23:22,437
(It passes the big sister's test.)

585
00:23:22,467 --> 00:23:24,407
(Sun Young grabs a piece of lettuce to make a wrap.)

586
00:23:24,567 --> 00:23:25,567
(trotters)

587
00:23:26,207 --> 00:23:27,307
(Ssamjang)

588
00:23:27,807 --> 00:23:29,207
(Dried radish)

589
00:23:29,477 --> 00:23:31,747
It's ready now.

590
00:23:32,477 --> 00:23:35,677
- You Seok's dish is delicious.
- Yes.

591
00:23:35,677 --> 00:23:37,687
- It tastes good in a wrap.
- Auntie.

592
00:23:38,217 --> 00:23:39,617
Do you want to bring some to the US?

593
00:23:40,147 --> 00:23:42,457
- In the US, - Gosh, sorry.

594
00:23:42,457 --> 00:23:43,557
you can't find things like this.

595
00:23:43,757 --> 00:23:45,357
Will you miss it in the US?

596
00:23:45,357 --> 00:23:46,387
Yes.

597
00:23:46,387 --> 00:23:47,527
(A taste that she'll miss in the US)

598
00:23:48,727 --> 00:23:51,397
(A combination of a spicy and sweet sauce and a chewy texture)

599
00:23:52,367 --> 00:23:53,997
(Good food is irresistible.)

600
00:23:54,097 --> 00:23:55,297
Gosh, sorry.

601
00:23:56,297 --> 00:23:59,107
(Trotters and dried radish are meant to be eaten together.)

602
00:24:02,177 --> 00:24:03,337
The dried radish.

603
00:24:03,507 --> 00:24:04,577
- Isn't it good?
- Yes.

604
00:24:05,107 --> 00:24:06,207
- It tastes good.
- Yes.

605
00:24:06,807 --> 00:24:08,047
The dried radish is good too.

606
00:24:08,277 --> 00:24:10,377
(Whoever made it, it's really good.)

607
00:24:11,347 --> 00:24:16,957
(Thanks to the dishes made by the youngest siblings,)

608
00:24:18,187 --> 00:24:19,187
(tonight's dinner has become even richer.)

609
00:24:19,187 --> 00:24:21,927
The trotters are really amazing.

610
00:24:22,927 --> 00:24:24,627
The eggs are perfectly boiled, too.

611
00:24:25,167 --> 00:24:27,297
- They're delicious.
- Yoon Seo did a good job.

612
00:24:27,297 --> 00:24:28,437
(Our youngest members can do it all.)

613
00:24:28,437 --> 00:24:30,437
Jung Ah, for simple dishes like these...

614
00:24:30,437 --> 00:24:31,467
Let's cook together.

615
00:24:31,467 --> 00:24:33,037
- These two can make them.
- We can divide up the menu.

616
00:24:33,037 --> 00:24:34,237
These two can handle them.

617
00:24:34,237 --> 00:24:36,037
I'll prep the ingredients really quickly.

618
00:24:36,277 --> 00:24:38,007
- That sounds good.
- They're good at making sauces too.

619
00:24:38,007 --> 00:24:39,177
Yes, they're both very good.

620
00:24:39,647 --> 00:24:41,277
I'll get better at cooking here.

621
00:24:43,177 --> 00:24:45,187
- Do you want them together?
- It's so good.

622
00:24:45,187 --> 00:24:46,847
(A bite of rice, and a bite of garlic scapes)

623
00:24:47,487 --> 00:24:48,657
It's delicious.

624
00:24:48,657 --> 00:24:49,687
(Three bites of garlic scapes)

625
00:24:50,017 --> 00:24:51,087
I love...

626
00:24:51,887 --> 00:24:52,927
garlic scapes.

627
00:24:54,927 --> 00:24:56,897
(The piquant taste and umami make it the perfect side dish for rice.)

628
00:24:56,897 --> 00:24:58,227
It's so good.

629
00:24:58,667 --> 00:25:01,267
(As she enjoys that satisfying crunch,)

630
00:25:02,137 --> 00:25:04,037
(the rice naturally follows.)

631
00:25:04,667 --> 00:25:08,137
(Jung Ah is also hooked on seasonal stir-fried garlic scapes.)

632
00:25:08,637 --> 00:25:10,707
(With the lingering umami filling their mouths)

633
00:25:10,977 --> 00:25:12,777
It's good with cucumber.

634
00:25:12,777 --> 00:25:14,847
(Their appetite explodes.)

635
00:25:16,117 --> 00:25:18,647
(You Seok picks up a perilla leaf.)

636
00:25:18,647 --> 00:25:19,717
Jung Ah.

637
00:25:20,347 --> 00:25:23,687
(Adding a slice of meat...)

638
00:25:24,657 --> 00:25:26,827
(and a piece of You Seok's pickled onion)

639
00:25:27,057 --> 00:25:29,297
- For Jung Ah who worked hard.
- Open up.

640
00:25:29,297 --> 00:25:30,767
Have a wrap.

641
00:25:31,027 --> 00:25:33,767
(Open up)

642
00:25:34,037 --> 00:25:35,597
(What about me?)

643
00:25:35,937 --> 00:25:37,197
How about a lettuce wrap?

644
00:25:37,197 --> 00:25:40,067
In the US, we like perilla leaves more than lettuce.

645
00:25:40,307 --> 00:25:42,007
In the US, people don't eat perilla leaves.

646
00:25:42,007 --> 00:25:43,237
- Wait. Hold on.
- In the US...

647
00:25:43,607 --> 00:25:44,707
Here's the thing about perilla leaves.

648
00:25:45,177 --> 00:25:46,847
- I know this one thing.
- I had no idea.

649
00:25:46,847 --> 00:25:48,777
Many foreigners think perilla leaves taste weird...

650
00:25:48,777 --> 00:25:49,977
- just like cilantro.
- That's true.

651
00:25:49,977 --> 00:25:51,817
- Not many eat perilla leaves.
- Because of its strong scent.

652
00:25:52,017 --> 00:25:53,247
Anyway, I'll make it with a perilla leaf.

653
00:25:53,247 --> 00:25:55,057
- In California, where I lived...
- I think...

654
00:25:55,357 --> 00:25:57,187
I think she's a fraud.

655
00:25:57,427 --> 00:25:59,857
She told me she got 1-on-1 lessons...

656
00:25:59,857 --> 00:26:01,197
from Matt Damon.

657
00:26:01,457 --> 00:26:02,627
- From Matt Damon?
- Yes.

658
00:26:02,627 --> 00:26:03,627
(Speechless)

659
00:26:03,727 --> 00:26:05,167
It was a wild boar, not Matt Damon.

660
00:26:05,767 --> 00:26:07,397
- A wild boar?
- She got lessons from a wild boar.

661
00:26:08,337 --> 00:26:09,997
(While they're laughing, a wrap for Jennica is ready.)

662
00:26:09,997 --> 00:26:11,767
Thank you very much.

663
00:26:15,977 --> 00:26:17,777
(Just watching Jennica makes me laugh.)

664
00:26:17,977 --> 00:26:19,177
This one is for our youngest member.

665
00:26:19,177 --> 00:26:20,547
- I'll make a wrap for Yoon Seo.
- Really?

666
00:26:20,547 --> 00:26:21,547
Yes.

667
00:26:21,547 --> 00:26:22,617
(Stuffing the vegetable wrap with so much delicious food)

668
00:26:22,617 --> 00:26:23,747
- Here you go.
- Perfect.

669
00:26:26,717 --> 00:26:27,787
There you go.

670
00:26:28,587 --> 00:26:30,487
I'll make one for You Seok this time.

671
00:26:30,487 --> 00:26:31,727
I'll make it.

672
00:26:31,727 --> 00:26:33,327
I'll put what I want in my own vegetable wrap.

673
00:26:33,327 --> 00:26:34,697
Really? Will you make one for me?

674
00:26:35,057 --> 00:26:36,197
I was going to do it by myself.

675
00:26:36,657 --> 00:26:39,197
(She makes a vegetable wrap for him in return.)

676
00:26:39,297 --> 00:26:40,297
Thank you.

677
00:26:41,697 --> 00:26:44,107
(Stuffing his mouth with the huge wrap)

678
00:26:44,837 --> 00:26:46,237
(The youngest members always bicker,)

679
00:26:46,237 --> 00:26:47,677
(but they look out for each other.)

680
00:26:48,107 --> 00:26:50,577
(Everything on the table is delicious.)

681
00:26:51,247 --> 00:26:54,177
(They can't stop eating.)

682
00:26:55,177 --> 00:27:00,647
(They enjoy tonight's dinner.)

683
00:27:01,887 --> 00:27:02,917
Seriously...

684
00:27:03,657 --> 00:27:05,087
I've been eating so well since we came here.

685
00:27:06,757 --> 00:27:08,557
When the viewers watch us eat...

686
00:27:09,327 --> 00:27:11,427
- They must be...
- If they haven't eaten anything,

687
00:27:11,427 --> 00:27:13,027
- they must crave this food.
- They can just get it delivered.

688
00:27:13,027 --> 00:27:15,037
- The delivery is so fast.
- Right. They can get it delivered.

689
00:27:15,037 --> 00:27:16,067
I think it's attached to this.

690
00:27:16,337 --> 00:27:17,967
(Scratching)

691
00:27:18,607 --> 00:27:19,937
Shall I remove the hair pieces now?

692
00:27:21,477 --> 00:27:22,907
It feels like...

693
00:27:23,137 --> 00:27:25,147
there's a bear on my head.

694
00:27:25,547 --> 00:27:27,477
It's time to say goodbye to the aunt from the US.

695
00:27:27,747 --> 00:27:30,477
Aunt Jennica is leaving for the US.

696
00:27:31,247 --> 00:27:32,287
Is she leaving now?

697
00:27:32,287 --> 00:27:34,087
- Yes, she's leaving.
- Aunt Jennica is leaving?

698
00:27:34,457 --> 00:27:36,387
I've never heard the name Jennica.

699
00:27:36,917 --> 00:27:38,127
- It's usually Jennifer or...
- It's...

700
00:27:38,127 --> 00:27:39,557
Jessica and another name got mixed up.

701
00:27:39,557 --> 00:27:40,557
- Jessica and...
- Jennifer.

702
00:27:42,197 --> 00:27:43,727
- I feel much better now.
- She's going back to being herself.

703
00:27:43,957 --> 00:27:46,327
- Sun Young, where have you been?
- Sun Young is back.

704
00:27:46,497 --> 00:27:48,067
Bye, Aunt Jennica.

705
00:27:48,567 --> 00:27:50,267
It feels good. It feels so refreshing.

706
00:27:51,007 --> 00:27:52,767
My lips are driving me crazy.

707
00:27:52,767 --> 00:27:54,007
(Meanwhile, Jung Ah's lips are driving her crazy.)

708
00:27:54,107 --> 00:27:55,577
The staying power of your lipstick is incredible.

709
00:27:55,907 --> 00:27:59,207
Your liner and lipstick are still intact.

710
00:27:59,207 --> 00:28:00,307
- They look just perfect.
- Indeed.

711
00:28:00,877 --> 00:28:03,017
Whenever I looked at you, I was amazed as you looked so pretty.

712
00:28:03,017 --> 00:28:04,587
Right. I know.

713
00:28:04,587 --> 00:28:05,717
The red lipstick.

714
00:28:06,187 --> 00:28:08,117
(Red)

715
00:28:08,117 --> 00:28:09,787
(Jeans)

716
00:28:10,057 --> 00:28:11,657
Isn't there a song about a red lipstick that goes like this?

717
00:28:12,057 --> 00:28:13,057
A red lipstick?

718
00:28:14,257 --> 00:28:15,697
(The youngest sings Lee Hi's "Red Lipstick," released in 2021.)

719
00:28:15,697 --> 00:28:17,597
- Is it an old song?
- "Pink Lipstick..."

720
00:28:17,597 --> 00:28:20,067
- There's "Pink Lipstick."
- Oh, "Pink Lipstick?"

721
00:28:22,067 --> 00:28:27,367
(The melody just slips out.)

722
00:28:27,907 --> 00:28:29,437
(I will forget tomorrow)

723
00:28:29,477 --> 00:28:31,847
- I will forget everything - I will forget everything

724
00:28:32,847 --> 00:28:34,247
(The song naturally transitions into another song.)

725
00:28:34,247 --> 00:28:35,647
("With Dark Lipstick" by Lim Ju Ri, 1987)

726
00:28:36,247 --> 00:28:37,717
- You don't know this song, right?
- No.

727
00:28:39,347 --> 00:28:40,747
- They really don't know...
- Does anyone know that song?

728
00:28:42,117 --> 00:28:46,027
(Immersed in the song)

729
00:28:46,457 --> 00:28:51,567
(The older members sing together.)

730
00:28:52,997 --> 00:28:54,337
What's the title of this song?

731
00:28:55,897 --> 00:28:57,567
(How come you don't know this song?)

732
00:28:57,567 --> 00:28:58,767
She's using the hair pieces as a mic.

733
00:28:59,267 --> 00:29:02,107
(Jennica turned into a mic.)

734
00:29:02,577 --> 00:29:04,247
You guys really don't know the song.

735
00:29:04,707 --> 00:29:06,177
Is it really okay for us to work together?

736
00:29:07,207 --> 00:29:09,217
They sure are from a different generation.

737
00:29:09,217 --> 00:29:10,347
(They finished dinner while feeling the generation gap.)

738
00:29:10,777 --> 00:29:12,647
(Sun Young came inside to tidy up.)

739
00:29:13,387 --> 00:29:14,687
Because we left the door open,

740
00:29:14,687 --> 00:29:16,217
there are like 1,000 moths in here.

741
00:29:16,787 --> 00:29:18,127
My gosh. A lot of them came inside.

742
00:29:18,127 --> 00:29:20,627
- Gosh. What is this...
- Did we leave the door open?

743
00:29:20,727 --> 00:29:22,957
- What's this mess?
- I wish we'd closed our room doors.

744
00:29:23,197 --> 00:29:25,527
This is a total mess. What should we do?

745
00:29:25,967 --> 00:29:28,797
Look up there. Those are all mosquitoes.

746
00:29:28,997 --> 00:29:30,667
What do we do?

747
00:29:30,767 --> 00:29:31,867
There are so many of them.

748
00:29:32,367 --> 00:29:33,967
- My gosh. Look at all those moths.
- Gosh, seriously.

749
00:29:34,167 --> 00:29:35,507
This is crazy.

750
00:29:36,337 --> 00:29:37,977
- We have to catch all of them.
- The window...

751
00:29:38,207 --> 00:29:39,207
Jung Ah.

752
00:29:39,347 --> 00:29:40,647
This is war against bugs.

753
00:29:41,377 --> 00:29:44,077
(Fresh Pest Control responds to the scene.)

754
00:29:44,487 --> 00:29:46,387
(The girls' room)

755
00:29:46,387 --> 00:29:48,187
(The living room)

756
00:29:48,817 --> 00:29:51,157
(Their only goal is the total extermination of bugs.)

757
00:29:51,657 --> 00:29:53,727
- It's funny that we're doing this.
- This is too much.

758
00:29:54,527 --> 00:29:58,027
(Jung Ah stays focused with the red lipstick still on.)

759
00:29:58,027 --> 00:29:59,067
(Swatting)

760
00:29:59,627 --> 00:30:00,697
There's a mosquito here.

761
00:30:01,237 --> 00:30:02,637
(Rushing)

762
00:30:02,897 --> 00:30:05,537
- Where is it?
- I caught it.

763
00:30:06,137 --> 00:30:07,167
I killed it.

764
00:30:07,707 --> 00:30:09,437
These bugs are coming out endlessly.

765
00:30:09,437 --> 00:30:12,747
(After spending a lot more time catching the bugs...)

766
00:30:14,647 --> 00:30:16,517
There will probably be even more bugs next month.

767
00:30:16,517 --> 00:30:17,887
(They clean up the mess as well. They're finally free from bugs.)

768
00:30:17,887 --> 00:30:18,887
Let's see how it turns out.

769
00:30:19,647 --> 00:30:21,817
We're caught all of them. I'm sure of it.

770
00:30:21,817 --> 00:30:23,417
(The war against bugs is over.)

771
00:30:23,517 --> 00:30:25,457
- Cheers, You Seok.
- Good job today.

772
00:30:25,457 --> 00:30:27,757
(They're finally having a relaxing time.)

773
00:30:28,427 --> 00:30:30,027
(Drowsy)

774
00:30:30,027 --> 00:30:31,267
Hey, are you sleepy?

775
00:30:31,367 --> 00:30:32,967
No, it's my eyes. My eyes are...

776
00:30:32,967 --> 00:30:35,367
- It's because of your eye makeup.
- I can just pop in some eye drops.

777
00:30:35,497 --> 00:30:37,437
- You didn't...
- I have eye drops for itchy eyes.

778
00:30:38,037 --> 00:30:39,537
- Just a second.
- I have eye drops.

779
00:30:40,467 --> 00:30:43,407
(You Seok rummages through his bag looking for something.)

780
00:30:43,577 --> 00:30:45,507
Hey, put this on before going to bed.

781
00:30:45,677 --> 00:30:47,047
- Oh, my. Thank you.
- You didn't...

782
00:30:47,047 --> 00:30:48,647
- You didn't do it last night.
- No, I didn't. Thank you.

783
00:30:48,777 --> 00:30:50,047
- Make sure to put it on.
- I'll take this.

784
00:30:50,047 --> 00:30:51,587
- I'm grateful for this.
- Put that warm eye mask on.

785
00:30:51,587 --> 00:30:52,717
I'm grateful for this.

786
00:30:53,347 --> 00:30:55,317
- You should take a shower.
- Exactly.

787
00:30:55,717 --> 00:30:56,787
You can take a shower first.

788
00:30:57,487 --> 00:30:58,687
I think she's done showering.

789
00:30:59,427 --> 00:31:00,427
Gosh. My back hurts.

790
00:31:00,757 --> 00:31:03,357
On our 1st trip, those 3 days...

791
00:31:03,927 --> 00:31:06,297
felt quite long in a good way. I could relax and enjoy the shoot.

792
00:31:06,967 --> 00:31:08,597
But the past three days here...

793
00:31:08,597 --> 00:31:10,597
- Time passed so quickly.
- Yes, indeed.

794
00:31:10,767 --> 00:31:12,807
- That must be why I feel this way.
- But as the shoot goes on,

795
00:31:12,907 --> 00:31:14,137
it'll feel like time is going by even more quickly.

796
00:31:14,477 --> 00:31:17,107
You're sad that the night is slipping away...

797
00:31:17,807 --> 00:31:23,277
(After tonight)

798
00:31:23,277 --> 00:31:25,987
(We'll have to part ways again)

799
00:31:25,987 --> 00:31:27,817
- The lyrics are just our story.
- Exactly.

800
00:31:28,817 --> 00:31:34,357
(The words of the song resonate deeply with them.)

801
00:31:35,327 --> 00:31:39,197
(Everyone is drenched in sadness.)

802
00:31:40,397 --> 00:31:42,167
This is my final look at the yard.

803
00:31:42,167 --> 00:31:43,967
It's sad. I really like this house.

804
00:31:44,367 --> 00:31:46,207
- This house is nice, isn't it?
- Yes, this one.

805
00:31:47,037 --> 00:31:49,437
- It's good.
- Stop looking at it now.

806
00:31:49,507 --> 00:31:52,577
You Seok, aren't you going to take a shower?

807
00:31:53,307 --> 00:31:56,117
- Come on. Leave him be.
- He just wants to...

808
00:31:56,117 --> 00:31:57,517
- Look at his hair.
- Earlier in the afternoon...

809
00:31:57,517 --> 00:32:00,087
- His hair is stiff from hairspray.
- Let me tell you something.

810
00:32:00,387 --> 00:32:02,057
- Go ahead.
- I can take a shower now.

811
00:32:02,917 --> 00:32:04,357
(Then go and take a shower.)

812
00:32:04,627 --> 00:32:07,557
- Go on. We'll wait for you.
- When I'm back, you'll be gone.

813
00:32:08,257 --> 00:32:09,257
(Crying out in sadness)

814
00:32:09,257 --> 00:32:11,427
- Oh, you're sad to say goodbye.
- When I'm back from the shower,

815
00:32:11,427 --> 00:32:12,967
you'll stay here for like five minutes...

816
00:32:12,967 --> 00:32:14,997
and then say we should all go to bed.

817
00:32:15,237 --> 00:32:17,337
- I'll wait until you go to bed.
- No.

818
00:32:17,497 --> 00:32:20,107
I hate that you're the only one here.

819
00:32:20,267 --> 00:32:22,107
What do you mean? Of course, I should take a shower by myself.

820
00:32:22,107 --> 00:32:23,207
No, I mean I hate that...

821
00:32:23,207 --> 00:32:24,337
you're the only dirty one here. Go and take a shower.

822
00:32:24,337 --> 00:32:26,047
I'm going to take a shower later.

823
00:32:26,047 --> 00:32:28,547
- I'm not saying I won't.
- When you're back from the shower,

824
00:32:28,547 --> 00:32:29,847
we can all have some beer together...

825
00:32:29,847 --> 00:32:30,847
- before going to bed.
- That's right.

826
00:32:30,847 --> 00:32:31,847
We don't have any beer left.

827
00:32:31,847 --> 00:32:33,717
- We still have beer.
- We have a lot of beer.

828
00:32:33,717 --> 00:32:35,457
- We still have beer.
- What's wrong with you?

829
00:32:35,457 --> 00:32:36,887
You guys are so loud.

830
00:32:37,417 --> 00:32:38,457
See?

831
00:32:38,457 --> 00:32:39,857
He likes to chat with us,

832
00:32:39,857 --> 00:32:41,457
so he's afraid we might go to bed early.

833
00:32:41,457 --> 00:32:43,127
- He's afraid of being left alone.
- He doesn't want us to be gone...

834
00:32:43,127 --> 00:32:44,927
- when he's back from the shower.
- He thinks we might be gone.

835
00:32:44,927 --> 00:32:46,197
- That's right.
- I see.

836
00:32:46,567 --> 00:32:47,997
I'll be waiting for you.

837
00:32:48,197 --> 00:32:50,267
I'll wait until you come back and then drink beer.

838
00:32:50,267 --> 00:32:52,807
- Are you going to drink more?
- Don't you worry.

839
00:32:52,807 --> 00:32:55,437
- I'll be back shortly.
- We won't leave you alone.

840
00:32:55,437 --> 00:32:57,177
(Finally, Anxiety goes to take a shower without worrying.)

841
00:32:58,147 --> 00:33:00,577
You Seok must be really sad to wrap this up.

842
00:33:01,917 --> 00:33:03,277
- You see, earlier...
- As if he had separation anxiety.

843
00:33:03,277 --> 00:33:04,547
He teared up earlier...

844
00:33:05,517 --> 00:33:07,917
while we were talking about how fast time passed by here.

845
00:33:08,457 --> 00:33:10,157
(He must be sad.)

846
00:33:10,257 --> 00:33:12,087
Does You Seok have no friends?

847
00:33:15,397 --> 00:33:16,427
Come on.

848
00:33:17,797 --> 00:33:19,397
Jung Ah, you're the logical type.

849
00:33:19,767 --> 00:33:21,837
You didn't even blink when I was crying.

850
00:33:22,037 --> 00:33:23,567
After our final shoot for "Love, Take Two,"

851
00:33:23,567 --> 00:33:24,667
you left without even looking back.

852
00:33:24,667 --> 00:33:25,737
It wasn't like that.

853
00:33:26,037 --> 00:33:27,707
- I just told you how he reacted.
- Then what was it?

854
00:33:28,007 --> 00:33:30,277
It doesn't change how I talk or act, does it?

855
00:33:31,207 --> 00:33:32,807
I was just stating the fact.

856
00:33:33,677 --> 00:33:36,017
Should we take him home with us?

857
00:33:36,547 --> 00:33:37,647
What should we do with him?

858
00:33:37,647 --> 00:33:39,817
He can stay at your place and mine for a month each.

859
00:33:40,547 --> 00:33:44,117
I don't think I can live with him for a month.

860
00:33:44,187 --> 00:33:45,827
- Really?
- My daughter will be uncomfortable.

861
00:33:45,827 --> 00:33:47,997
After we finish the final shoot, You Seok will...

862
00:33:48,727 --> 00:33:50,997
(You Seok comes back after the shower.)

863
00:33:51,997 --> 00:33:53,027
(Spotting something)

864
00:33:53,027 --> 00:33:54,427
You said you wouldn't drink it before I came back.

865
00:33:55,297 --> 00:33:57,337
- It wasn't my decision.
- It's not a big deal.

866
00:33:57,667 --> 00:33:58,807
Gosh, seriously.

867
00:33:58,807 --> 00:34:00,137
- I promised...
- I knew it.

868
00:34:00,137 --> 00:34:01,607
I made a promise to you.

869
00:34:01,837 --> 00:34:03,977
- But Choon Ja...
- It wasn't like that.

870
00:34:04,337 --> 00:34:06,307
We have to wake up at 8:30am.

871
00:34:06,307 --> 00:34:07,807
- We have to wake up then?
- Yes.

872
00:34:08,047 --> 00:34:10,277
- You can get up at 9am.
- Okay.

873
00:34:10,277 --> 00:34:12,017
- Then I'll get up at 9am.
- All right.

874
00:34:12,417 --> 00:34:14,117
I have to wait until my kids come home before going to bed.

875
00:34:14,117 --> 00:34:15,117
Right.

876
00:34:15,117 --> 00:34:16,617
No, that's not the case.

877
00:34:17,887 --> 00:34:22,827
(They didn't waste a single moment of their second night in Taean.)

878
00:34:23,397 --> 00:34:26,767
(And the next day)

879
00:34:27,427 --> 00:34:33,567
(Everyone is still sleeping soundly.)

880
00:34:34,007 --> 00:34:35,507
(Scratching)

881
00:34:36,637 --> 00:34:40,607
(He falls back asleep.)

882
00:34:41,377 --> 00:34:46,347
(It's another peaceful morning.)

883
00:34:47,147 --> 00:34:49,617
(Current time: 8:27am)

884
00:34:49,617 --> 00:34:51,957
(There's about 1 hour left until wake-up time.)

885
00:34:52,727 --> 00:34:55,927
(At the same time, in the yard...)

886
00:34:56,397 --> 00:35:00,097
(The staff members are moving around suspiciously.)

887
00:35:00,427 --> 00:35:03,767
(They carefully enter the yard.)

888
00:35:04,067 --> 00:35:07,007
(They're preparing something secretly.)

889
00:35:07,867 --> 00:35:13,447
(The cast members are sleeping soundly.)

890
00:35:14,207 --> 00:35:15,217
(Cock-a-doodle-doo)

891
00:35:22,817 --> 00:35:23,917
What's going on?

892
00:35:25,127 --> 00:35:27,997
(Am I dreaming?)

893
00:35:28,527 --> 00:35:29,557
What's going on?

894
00:35:30,057 --> 00:35:31,157
My gosh. That...

895
00:35:32,067 --> 00:35:33,167
That startled me to death.

896
00:35:33,327 --> 00:35:35,867
(Now that she's awake, she does techno dance.)

897
00:35:35,867 --> 00:35:36,867
What time is it now?

898
00:35:38,837 --> 00:35:39,937
But at 9:30am...

899
00:35:40,337 --> 00:35:42,807
- At 9:30am... Sorry?
- We were going to make breakfast.

900
00:35:42,807 --> 00:35:44,237
We planned to make breakfast at 9:30am.

901
00:35:44,237 --> 00:35:45,777
(Trying to figure out the situation in their natural state)

902
00:35:46,347 --> 00:35:48,577
(The staff makes an announcement.)

903
00:35:48,577 --> 00:35:49,577
Sorry?

904
00:35:50,147 --> 00:35:51,147
I can't hear you.

905
00:35:53,417 --> 00:35:55,217
- What did you say?
- What did she say?

906
00:35:55,217 --> 00:35:56,657
I haven't even drawn on my eyebrows.

907
00:35:56,657 --> 00:35:57,787
(The quiet yard suddenly turned into a club.)

908
00:35:57,787 --> 00:35:58,857
What did you say?

909
00:35:58,857 --> 00:36:00,857
(The quiet yard suddenly turned into a club.)

910
00:36:01,157 --> 00:36:03,327
(Perking up his ears in front of the door)

911
00:36:03,427 --> 00:36:06,867
(Jung Ah and Yoon Seo, please wake up immediately.)

912
00:36:07,127 --> 00:36:09,337
You said we could sleep until 9:30am.

913
00:36:09,497 --> 00:36:10,837
(Upset)

914
00:36:11,097 --> 00:36:12,807
Jung Ah and Yoon Seo,

915
00:36:12,807 --> 00:36:15,107
please wake up immediately.

916
00:36:15,377 --> 00:36:17,577
What's their problem? This is driving me crazy.

917
00:36:18,907 --> 00:36:19,907
This is ridiculous.

918
00:36:20,347 --> 00:36:22,517
(Laughing)

919
00:36:22,647 --> 00:36:24,017
- You woke me up...
- You're ridiculous.

920
00:36:24,017 --> 00:36:26,117
Why would you tell us a lie?

921
00:36:26,647 --> 00:36:27,787
What's wrong with you?

922
00:36:29,287 --> 00:36:30,717
Oh, I get it.

923
00:36:31,387 --> 00:36:32,757
- It's only 8:30am...
- I just figured it out.

924
00:36:32,757 --> 00:36:33,827
What is it?

925
00:36:35,257 --> 00:36:36,297
Guys.

926
00:36:36,997 --> 00:36:37,997
It's what we did yesterday.

927
00:36:38,397 --> 00:36:40,467
- Had we known, we wouldn't have...
- I can't find my shoes.

928
00:36:40,467 --> 00:36:41,467
(Grumbling)

929
00:36:41,467 --> 00:36:42,597
drunk beer last night.

930
00:36:43,237 --> 00:36:45,767
(Messy hair)

931
00:36:45,767 --> 00:36:46,837
Right, Jung Ah?

932
00:36:46,867 --> 00:36:48,107
Of course.

933
00:36:48,307 --> 00:36:50,807
I have no makeup on.

934
00:36:51,607 --> 00:36:54,507
What's going on? Why would you lie to us?

935
00:36:54,507 --> 00:36:56,147
(You said the wake-up time was 9:30am.)

936
00:36:56,517 --> 00:36:57,577
They're liars.

937
00:36:59,117 --> 00:37:01,457
- What do you want us to do?
- Shall we give them another chance?

938
00:37:01,457 --> 00:37:02,987
Yesterday,

939
00:37:03,117 --> 00:37:06,127
you dressed up in retro style and posed for photos.

940
00:37:06,127 --> 00:37:08,957
- Yes.
- The staff members had a poll...

941
00:37:08,957 --> 00:37:11,727
with those photos of yours yesterday.

942
00:37:11,727 --> 00:37:13,997
- What poll? Gosh, seriously.
- I told you so.

943
00:37:14,067 --> 00:37:15,237
You had a poll?

944
00:37:17,297 --> 00:37:20,167
(Just a day ago, they took a peaceful family photoshoot.)

945
00:37:21,307 --> 00:37:25,307
(They thought it was to make good memories.)

946
00:37:25,947 --> 00:37:29,047
(But with their individual photos,)

947
00:37:29,947 --> 00:37:33,747
(the secret poll began among the staff members.)

948
00:37:33,987 --> 00:37:37,517
(My goodness! Who's the best dresser that impressed you?)

949
00:37:37,957 --> 00:37:39,627
(Contestant 1: Jung Ah)

950
00:37:39,987 --> 00:37:41,497
(The 1970s' modern girl with romantic and unconventional vibes!)

951
00:37:41,727 --> 00:37:43,327
(Passionate red stockings)

952
00:37:43,727 --> 00:37:46,427
(Yum Jung Ah, the original Miss Korea diva)

953
00:37:47,897 --> 00:37:48,997
(Contestant 2: Jennica)

954
00:37:49,267 --> 00:37:51,297
Yes, this is the true scent of Korea.

955
00:37:51,297 --> 00:37:52,437
(The icon of the 1970s hippie vibe, soaked in American culture)

956
00:37:52,867 --> 00:37:54,837
(Jennica, the aunt who returned from the US)

957
00:37:55,707 --> 00:37:57,907
(Contestant 3: You James Dean)

958
00:37:58,177 --> 00:38:01,677
(The double denim look and a red scarf)

959
00:38:02,317 --> 00:38:03,947
(You James Dean, the Western tough guy)

960
00:38:04,787 --> 00:38:06,517
(Contestant 4: Roh Yoon Sunny)

961
00:38:06,917 --> 00:38:09,257
(The bold mix of denim overalls and a red bandana is the key feature.)

962
00:38:09,657 --> 00:38:12,957
(Roh Yoon Sunny from the girl group S.O.S)

963
00:38:13,727 --> 00:38:17,127
(The 1st Siblings' Fashion Leader Contest)

964
00:38:17,497 --> 00:38:19,727
Vote for the best fashion leader. Each one has one vote.

965
00:38:19,727 --> 00:38:20,927
(The contestants' fate depends on the voting results.)

966
00:38:21,067 --> 00:38:22,997
- She's sweeping the votes.
- This is the true retro style.

967
00:38:23,367 --> 00:38:24,937
- I'm voting for the red colour.
- The red colour?

968
00:38:25,737 --> 00:38:27,437
The double denim look is the ultimate fashion style.

969
00:38:27,607 --> 00:38:29,207
The face is what completes a fashion style.

970
00:38:30,277 --> 00:38:31,677
- I'm voting for Jung Ah.
- I choose Sun Young.

971
00:38:31,977 --> 00:38:33,207
I'm voting for You Seok.

972
00:38:33,577 --> 00:38:35,877
- Yoon Seo looks great.
- I'm voting for Yoon Seo.

973
00:38:36,517 --> 00:38:39,587
(It continued until sunset. Here are the results.)

974
00:38:39,817 --> 00:38:41,687
(My goodness! Who's the best dresser that impressed you?)

975
00:38:41,687 --> 00:38:44,417
(Jung Ah: 22, Sun Young: 34, You Seok: 25, Yoon Seo: 17)

976
00:38:44,587 --> 00:38:45,587
(3rd place, 1st place, 2nd place, 4th place)

977
00:38:45,587 --> 00:38:48,797
(Jung Ah and Yoon Seo are in the bottom two.)

978
00:38:50,197 --> 00:38:53,327
The bottom two are going for additional work today.

979
00:38:53,327 --> 00:38:55,267
Additional work?

980
00:38:56,337 --> 00:38:59,407
(We're saved.)

981
00:39:00,007 --> 00:39:01,807
(Jumping up and down with joy)

982
00:39:01,807 --> 00:39:04,177
- Sun Young, we made it.
- You Seok, great job.

983
00:39:04,177 --> 00:39:06,147
- Is that why you called us out?
- Yes.

984
00:39:06,807 --> 00:39:08,377
(Closing her eyes)

985
00:39:08,877 --> 00:39:10,377
(She's in denial.)

986
00:39:11,217 --> 00:39:16,117
(Aunt Jennica's style was unbeatable.)

987
00:39:17,357 --> 00:39:19,527
(Satisfied)

988
00:39:19,527 --> 00:39:22,397
The 2 of you have 5 minutes to get ready.

989
00:39:22,397 --> 00:39:24,457
- Come on. Five minutes?
- Five minutes is too short.

990
00:39:24,457 --> 00:39:25,467
(The cut throat world of competition)

991
00:39:25,467 --> 00:39:27,127
We'll give you ten minutes. Hurry up.

992
00:39:27,567 --> 00:39:29,037
- You Seok.
- We harvested onions.

993
00:39:29,037 --> 00:39:31,967
- My advice was helpful, wasn't it?
- I'm glad I took your advice.

994
00:39:31,967 --> 00:39:33,937
- You should be.
- We're saved.

995
00:39:33,937 --> 00:39:35,337
That's right. You did well.

996
00:39:36,207 --> 00:39:38,877
By the way, where did that noise come from?

997
00:39:39,577 --> 00:39:41,817
The noise from earlier. It terrified me.

998
00:39:43,647 --> 00:39:45,087
I thought I was having a nightmare.

999
00:39:45,987 --> 00:39:47,047
Play it one more time.

1000
00:39:47,047 --> 00:39:48,817
(She chuckles as she says, "Play it one more time.")

1001
00:39:49,457 --> 00:39:51,187
(Here goes "Cock-A-Doodle-Doo Song" once again.)

1002
00:39:53,157 --> 00:39:54,187
What now?

1003
00:39:56,827 --> 00:40:00,167
(What now? What is it?)

1004
00:40:02,337 --> 00:40:07,407
(They already got used to "Cock-A-Doodle-Doo Song.")

1005
00:40:07,837 --> 00:40:09,737
This song is so exciting.

1006
00:40:11,807 --> 00:40:14,977
I thought it was going too peacefully.

1007
00:40:15,447 --> 00:40:18,417
I get it. It's clear now. On the last day,

1008
00:40:18,887 --> 00:40:21,787
two of us are bound to get dragged somewhere for extra work.

1009
00:40:22,387 --> 00:40:24,087
- It was the same last time. Right?
- Yes.

1010
00:40:25,157 --> 00:40:26,227
What a relief. We're saved.

1011
00:40:26,657 --> 00:40:29,327
There must be tension in the air in that room right now.

1012
00:40:29,327 --> 00:40:31,867
I'll stay here until Jung Ah leaves.

1013
00:40:31,867 --> 00:40:33,227
(She's now walking on eggshells.)

1014
00:40:34,167 --> 00:40:35,397
(At the same time, the girls' room)

1015
00:40:35,397 --> 00:40:37,667
But why are we in the bottom two?

1016
00:40:38,467 --> 00:40:39,537
I have nothing to say about that.

1017
00:40:41,267 --> 00:40:42,577
(Laughing)

1018
00:40:43,877 --> 00:40:45,207
I hate you, Sun Young.

1019
00:40:46,147 --> 00:40:47,347
(Laughing)

1020
00:40:47,807 --> 00:40:49,347
Gosh. I'm so upset.

1021
00:40:49,647 --> 00:40:52,317
Sun Young, don't laugh at us.

1022
00:40:52,317 --> 00:40:53,417
(Laughing)

1023
00:40:53,417 --> 00:40:54,447
Sun Young.

1024
00:40:54,447 --> 00:40:55,457
Be safe. I'll see you later.

1025
00:40:55,957 --> 00:40:56,987
- Shall I give you a massage?
- It will be tough.

1026
00:40:56,987 --> 00:40:57,987
Forget it!

1027
00:40:58,587 --> 00:41:01,257
I'm not upset about going there.

1028
00:41:01,587 --> 00:41:03,827
- Then what?
- How come You Seok beat me...

1029
00:41:04,427 --> 00:41:06,297
- Gosh.
- Is that what you're upset about?

1030
00:41:06,297 --> 00:41:07,327
That's what I'm upset about.

1031
00:41:07,467 --> 00:41:08,767
But I really did my best yesterday.

1032
00:41:09,437 --> 00:41:11,837
Maybe my vibe... I think I beat you with my energy.

1033
00:41:11,937 --> 00:41:13,367
- You Seok. Hey.
- Yes?

1034
00:41:13,367 --> 00:41:14,907
- Be quiet and fold the blankets.
- Okay.

1035
00:41:16,037 --> 00:41:18,507
- Read the room, will you?
- Okay.

1036
00:41:18,507 --> 00:41:20,347
Get up right now.

1037
00:41:21,107 --> 00:41:22,777
Jung Ah must be really tired now.

1038
00:41:23,777 --> 00:41:26,747
- Gosh, I'm upset.
- You don't seem upset.

1039
00:41:26,917 --> 00:41:29,557
You don't look upset at all.

1040
00:41:29,817 --> 00:41:31,357
Sun Young is so happy right now...

1041
00:41:31,357 --> 00:41:33,127
that she's smiling from ear to ear.

1042
00:41:33,127 --> 00:41:35,457
You guys won't be just chilling either.

1043
00:41:35,597 --> 00:41:38,597
- We should make breakfast.
- We'll make delicious dishes.

1044
00:41:39,297 --> 00:41:41,627
- Anything will be fine.
- We should make something nice.

1045
00:41:42,267 --> 00:41:44,537
(They're ready to go to work.)

1046
00:41:44,537 --> 00:41:46,907
By the way, how many votes did I get?

1047
00:41:47,767 --> 00:41:49,807
I was supposed to at least place second.

1048
00:41:51,377 --> 00:41:54,977
It's because I didn't look funny. I looked just pretty. Right?

1049
00:41:55,477 --> 00:41:56,477
Because I didn't look funny, right?

1050
00:41:57,617 --> 00:42:00,047
(Absolutely)

1051
00:42:00,617 --> 00:42:04,117
(She failed because she looked too pretty.)

1052
00:42:05,157 --> 00:42:06,657
- Let's get going, Yoon Seo.
- Okay.

1053
00:42:07,457 --> 00:42:09,097
(Receiving a beverage from You Seok)

1054
00:42:09,097 --> 00:42:10,627
- See you later.
- See you later.

1055
00:42:10,927 --> 00:42:12,997
- Should we go now?
- Jung Ah, see you later.

1056
00:42:13,197 --> 00:42:15,237
- Bye, Yoon Seo.
- Come back in one piece.

1057
00:42:16,097 --> 00:42:17,997
Sun Young, you swept the votes.

1058
00:42:18,507 --> 00:42:20,137
(He checks the rankings to the last moment.)

1059
00:42:20,567 --> 00:42:23,277
(Jung Ah and Yoon Seo head to the unknown workplace.)

1060
00:42:23,707 --> 00:42:24,877
It must be potato or...

1061
00:42:25,547 --> 00:42:28,047
He mentioned a chicken farm because of the chicken song.

1062
00:42:29,017 --> 00:42:30,717
Blue crab? No, I don't think that's it.

1063
00:42:30,717 --> 00:42:31,747
(Or blue crab?)

1064
00:42:32,217 --> 00:42:35,117
(Where is today's workplace that awaits the two of them?)

1065
00:42:35,517 --> 00:42:37,187
Yes, we're going. It's just...

1066
00:42:37,417 --> 00:42:40,027
I had a feeling that we wouldn't be just chilling before going home.

1067
00:42:41,557 --> 00:42:42,857
I wonder where we're heading.

1068
00:42:42,857 --> 00:42:43,897
(Where are they being dragged to?)

1069
00:42:44,497 --> 00:42:47,997
(What place will they be working at?)

1070
00:42:48,431 --> 00:42:49,861
(Current time: 8:50am)

1071
00:42:50,291 --> 00:42:51,631
(The winners are enjoying a relaxing time.)

1072
00:42:53,061 --> 00:42:55,501
(Yawning)

1073
00:42:55,801 --> 00:42:57,771
(How much longer will you keep yawning?)

1074
00:42:58,501 --> 00:43:00,771
(She's letting out a long yawn, looking so relaxed.)

1075
00:43:00,771 --> 00:43:02,841
Oh, my. This is so nice.

1076
00:43:03,671 --> 00:43:06,141
I had no idea not working could feel...

1077
00:43:06,141 --> 00:43:07,411
this good.

1078
00:43:08,911 --> 00:43:10,551
(Yawning)

1079
00:43:10,951 --> 00:43:12,921
(She gives another long yawn.)

1080
00:43:13,581 --> 00:43:15,921
(And then, she makes iced coffee in a relaxed manner.)

1081
00:43:16,362 --> 00:43:17,402
Viewers,

1082
00:43:18,202 --> 00:43:20,032
I've been chosen.

1083
00:43:20,572 --> 00:43:21,632
I placed first.

1084
00:43:21,632 --> 00:43:24,142
(Happy)

1085
00:43:24,402 --> 00:43:25,472
(Giggling)

1086
00:43:25,912 --> 00:43:27,342
(He stops and watches her in sheer joy.)

1087
00:43:27,342 --> 00:43:28,442
- How about a cup of...
- What are you doing?

1088
00:43:29,012 --> 00:43:31,642
- Sun Young, you...
- I was bragging to the viewers.

1089
00:43:31,642 --> 00:43:32,682
But...

1090
00:43:34,314 --> 00:43:36,754
Unbelievable. Sun Young, come over here.

1091
00:43:37,384 --> 00:43:38,484
Come to think of it,

1092
00:43:39,084 --> 00:43:41,024
you placed 1st, and I placed 2nd at the curry showdown too.

1093
00:43:41,894 --> 00:43:44,024
- That's right.
- You always place first.

1094
00:43:44,024 --> 00:43:45,094
(The deity of victory is on our side.)

1095
00:43:45,624 --> 00:43:46,624
I just realised it.

1096
00:43:46,964 --> 00:43:49,034
We have good energy. We should stick together.

1097
00:43:49,034 --> 00:43:50,964
Exactly. We should...

1098
00:43:51,394 --> 00:43:53,534
- But if we keep winning...
- You dropped this.

1099
00:43:53,534 --> 00:43:55,834
We should look after Yoon Seo since she's the youngest.

1100
00:43:55,834 --> 00:43:58,174
- Let's help her from now on.
- Okay.

1101
00:43:58,174 --> 00:43:59,704
- Let's help her win next time.
- Okay.

1102
00:43:59,704 --> 00:44:02,474
We should take better care of the youngest member.

1103
00:44:02,674 --> 00:44:03,744
- Right?
- Yes.

1104
00:44:03,744 --> 00:44:06,214
- Starting from the next shoot, - Should I work instead of her?

1105
00:44:06,214 --> 00:44:09,254
- do worse than her no matter what.
- No.

1106
00:44:09,354 --> 00:44:10,514
- I'll do my best to win.
- No.

1107
00:44:10,514 --> 00:44:12,084
- Yoon Seo and I...
- What about Yoon Seo?

1108
00:44:12,084 --> 00:44:13,154
- She...
- Do you want her to work again?

1109
00:44:13,154 --> 00:44:15,194
- She and I can be in the top two.
- Okay.

1110
00:44:15,194 --> 00:44:16,254
And you should work.

1111
00:44:16,754 --> 00:44:17,994
I'm not sure I can do that.

1112
00:44:18,764 --> 00:44:21,894
(I'll be in the first place no matter what.)

1113
00:44:22,734 --> 00:44:23,764
(Let's just enjoy this relaxing time for now.)

1114
00:44:23,764 --> 00:44:24,834
That's funny.

1115
00:44:25,564 --> 00:44:27,364
(Yoon Seo washed up and is feeling refreshed.)

1116
00:44:27,764 --> 00:44:28,974
- Sun Young.
- Yes?

1117
00:44:29,634 --> 00:44:30,904
Are we going to start cooking at 9am?

1118
00:44:31,904 --> 00:44:33,644
- Why? Are you the planning type?
- No.

1119
00:44:34,244 --> 00:44:35,374
Can I do some exercise?

1120
00:44:36,174 --> 00:44:37,174
(He'll exercise instead of cooking?)

1121
00:44:37,174 --> 00:44:38,214
At 9am?

1122
00:44:38,214 --> 00:44:39,344
I'm going out for a jog until 9am.

1123
00:44:39,344 --> 00:44:40,814
Okay, I don't mind.

1124
00:44:41,184 --> 00:44:42,514
But after I'm back by 9am,

1125
00:44:42,784 --> 00:44:44,484
showering will take ten minutes. Is that okay?

1126
00:44:44,654 --> 00:44:45,654
I'm fine with it.

1127
00:44:46,084 --> 00:44:47,254
We've got plenty of time.

1128
00:44:47,254 --> 00:44:49,354
- That's right.
- Okay, I'm off.

1129
00:44:49,724 --> 00:44:50,994
I'm off for a jog.

1130
00:44:51,694 --> 00:44:52,764
Jung Ah and...

1131
00:44:54,024 --> 00:44:55,894
Yoon Seo have gone to work.

1132
00:44:56,364 --> 00:44:58,464
It can't be helped. Those who won have a life too.

1133
00:44:59,604 --> 00:45:00,964
Hi, this is You Seok.

1134
00:45:01,704 --> 00:45:02,704
Today...

1135
00:45:02,704 --> 00:45:03,874
(He's even shooting a solo video.)

1136
00:45:03,874 --> 00:45:05,074
While jogging, I'll show you...

1137
00:45:05,544 --> 00:45:08,304
nature, the sky,

1138
00:45:08,944 --> 00:45:10,774
and me.

1139
00:45:11,774 --> 00:45:13,344
(Leaving meal prep for later, he heads to the beach.)

1140
00:45:13,344 --> 00:45:14,544
Nature is a must...

1141
00:45:14,944 --> 00:45:16,114
for people.

1142
00:45:18,114 --> 00:45:22,924
(You Seok arrived at a nearby beach.)

1143
00:45:22,924 --> 00:45:24,594
(A video is a must.)

1144
00:45:24,954 --> 00:45:26,094
What a superb view.

1145
00:45:28,064 --> 00:45:31,434
(A wide-open sea that refreshes the soul)

1146
00:45:34,334 --> 00:45:35,774
Look at how clear the water is.

1147
00:45:36,874 --> 00:45:39,604
(Even the crystal-clear, shimmering seawater)

1148
00:45:41,244 --> 00:45:43,574
(While he relaxes and enjoys the moment,)

1149
00:45:43,574 --> 00:45:45,914
(forgetting all about making breakfast)

1150
00:45:46,284 --> 00:45:49,214
I'm going to draw my eyebrows.

1151
00:45:49,214 --> 00:45:50,754
This is me trying to draw my eyebrows.

1152
00:45:50,784 --> 00:45:52,484
Because I look too pale,

1153
00:45:52,524 --> 00:45:55,554
I'm doing this to remove extra makeup.

1154
00:45:55,554 --> 00:45:56,894
(Kim Sun Young's "Get It Beauty")

1155
00:45:56,894 --> 00:45:58,724
Think of it as giving them some depth.

1156
00:45:59,924 --> 00:46:01,464
My makeup artist said...

1157
00:46:02,434 --> 00:46:03,894
to start with my right.

1158
00:46:05,204 --> 00:46:06,864
(With idling away so much,)

1159
00:46:06,864 --> 00:46:09,504
(can they make breakfast before Jung Ah and Yoon Seo come?)

1160
00:46:09,734 --> 00:46:10,804
A doggy.

1161
00:46:11,034 --> 00:46:12,204
Where are we? What are we doing?

1162
00:46:14,344 --> 00:46:15,644
(Clucking)

1163
00:46:15,644 --> 00:46:17,314
The sound of chickens is...

1164
00:46:17,314 --> 00:46:18,584
I can actually hear chickens.

1165
00:46:19,044 --> 00:46:20,414
- It's chickens.
- Really?

1166
00:46:20,414 --> 00:46:21,844
(A place with chickens clucking?)

1167
00:46:22,314 --> 00:46:27,854
(This very place where chickens happily roam free)

1168
00:46:28,894 --> 00:46:31,524
(Sure-footed strides)

1169
00:46:33,164 --> 00:46:36,634
(A proud comb)

1170
00:46:38,534 --> 00:46:40,234
(A plump rear)

1171
00:46:41,904 --> 00:46:44,474
(Today's workplace: A chicken farm)

1172
00:46:45,844 --> 00:46:48,974
Chicken? What could we do with them? Collect eggs?

1173
00:46:49,614 --> 00:46:50,714
Chickens...

1174
00:46:50,914 --> 00:46:52,784
- It'll be my first...
- Aren't we scared of chickens?

1175
00:46:52,784 --> 00:46:53,944
It'll be my first time seeing real chickens.

1176
00:46:53,944 --> 00:46:55,284
(Worried even before encountering the chickens)

1177
00:46:55,814 --> 00:46:57,684
(Carefully entering the chickens' home)

1178
00:46:58,184 --> 00:46:59,524
Could that chicken be the boss?

1179
00:46:59,654 --> 00:47:01,154
What do we do with these guys?

1180
00:47:01,784 --> 00:47:03,454
Here, you'll be collecting...

1181
00:47:03,924 --> 00:47:06,564
fertilized eggs with shell number one.

1182
00:47:06,664 --> 00:47:07,994
Nice.

1183
00:47:08,294 --> 00:47:09,564
Can we take some home?

1184
00:47:09,994 --> 00:47:11,064
- Really?
- Number one.

1185
00:47:11,064 --> 00:47:12,464
I always buy number one eggs.

1186
00:47:13,634 --> 00:47:15,104
(A chicken farm in the heart of nature)

1187
00:47:15,104 --> 00:47:18,104
As you can see, I let the chickens roam around freely.

1188
00:47:18,104 --> 00:47:21,004
I never close the chicken coop doors.

1189
00:47:21,004 --> 00:47:22,674
(Free-range chickens raised with the coop doors left open)

1190
00:47:22,874 --> 00:47:24,614
They get to eat what they want...

1191
00:47:24,614 --> 00:47:27,284
and lay eggs when they want to. That's how they're kept.

1192
00:47:28,184 --> 00:47:31,384
(That's what makes these...)

1193
00:47:31,384 --> 00:47:35,394
(number 1 shell-marked eggs possible.)

1194
00:47:35,524 --> 00:47:36,594
Hi.

1195
00:47:36,824 --> 00:47:38,324
- Hi.
- Hi.

1196
00:47:38,454 --> 00:47:40,524
- Are you here for the eggs?
- Yes.

1197
00:47:40,524 --> 00:47:43,334
My gosh. I can't give them to you for free.

1198
00:47:43,334 --> 00:47:44,364
No, of course not.

1199
00:47:44,364 --> 00:47:45,964
- First, the chickens...
- They must be fed first.

1200
00:47:45,964 --> 00:47:46,964
Correct.

1201
00:47:47,234 --> 00:47:49,274
(On the way to cut grass for the chickens)

1202
00:47:49,274 --> 00:47:51,004
We're heading to where the grass is.

1203
00:47:51,004 --> 00:47:52,544
That's where pumpkins were planted.

1204
00:47:53,404 --> 00:47:55,414
The pumpkins will be harvested in autumn...

1205
00:47:55,414 --> 00:47:57,244
for the chickens to eat in winter.

1206
00:47:57,474 --> 00:47:59,584
Is this field for the chickens' food?

1207
00:47:59,584 --> 00:48:01,184
Yes, solely to feed the chickens.

1208
00:48:01,344 --> 00:48:02,654
They sure eat the good stuff.

1209
00:48:02,984 --> 00:48:05,054
- Right? They eat...
- The chickens eat quality food.

1210
00:48:05,054 --> 00:48:08,054
So the eggs are from chickens that eat quality food.

1211
00:48:10,094 --> 00:48:12,324
(Arrived at the grass-cutting spot)

1212
00:48:12,324 --> 00:48:13,424
Leave the cart here.

1213
00:48:14,564 --> 00:48:16,364
- Let me demonstrate.
- Okay.

1214
00:48:16,494 --> 00:48:19,704
You may hurt your hand if you grab the grass...

1215
00:48:19,704 --> 00:48:21,064
too close to the bottom.

1216
00:48:21,064 --> 00:48:23,774
Grab the grass around here and cut it.

1217
00:48:24,934 --> 00:48:25,974
(A few swipes of the sickle, and it's done.)

1218
00:48:25,974 --> 00:48:27,274
Do we not pull the roots out?

1219
00:48:27,274 --> 00:48:28,574
You can just cut the top parts.

1220
00:48:29,614 --> 00:48:31,614
- Does it grow back?
- Yes, it does.

1221
00:48:31,614 --> 00:48:34,084
Please fill a whole cart with grass.

1222
00:48:34,214 --> 00:48:35,884
- Okay.
- Like so. Try it.

1223
00:48:36,584 --> 00:48:38,084
(The two cut grass as instructed.)

1224
00:48:38,084 --> 00:48:40,454
Be careful of the sickle when you pull it towards you.

1225
00:48:40,454 --> 00:48:41,454
Got it.

1226
00:48:42,294 --> 00:48:45,724
(Cutting grass? It's not hard.)

1227
00:48:47,224 --> 00:48:49,764
(Cutting one blade of grass after another and stacking it up)

1228
00:48:49,764 --> 00:48:50,864
Like this.

1229
00:48:54,104 --> 00:48:56,774
(The two fill up the cart diligently.)

1230
00:48:57,704 --> 00:48:58,804
Grass like this one?

1231
00:48:58,804 --> 00:49:00,574
(Meanwhile, Yoon Seo is...)

1232
00:49:01,744 --> 00:49:03,814
What kind of grass is this? It looks interesting.

1233
00:49:04,344 --> 00:49:05,914
It sure looks interesting.

1234
00:49:07,214 --> 00:49:08,984
(Exclaiming)

1235
00:49:09,784 --> 00:49:12,724
(Yoon Seo also works hard.)

1236
00:49:13,454 --> 00:49:15,154
(The more they cut,)

1237
00:49:15,154 --> 00:49:17,454
(the more grass is stacking up for the chickens' snack.)

1238
00:49:17,854 --> 00:49:20,594
Like this.

1239
00:49:20,594 --> 00:49:21,594
(Tug-of-war with the grass)

1240
00:49:21,894 --> 00:49:22,964
Like this.

1241
00:49:22,964 --> 00:49:25,834
(Yoon Seo got the trophy after much tug-of-war.)

1242
00:49:26,804 --> 00:49:28,234
(Groaning)

1243
00:49:28,234 --> 00:49:29,234
(Groaning)

1244
00:49:29,634 --> 00:49:31,774
(A handful after much trouble)

1245
00:49:31,774 --> 00:49:33,944
Thinking how the chickens will enjoy this...

1246
00:49:33,944 --> 00:49:34,944
(Becoming energetic at the thought of feeding the chickens)

1247
00:49:34,944 --> 00:49:36,514
- It's nice.
- Expensive grass?

1248
00:49:37,044 --> 00:49:38,784
- So they can eat it more easily?
- Yes.

1249
00:49:38,784 --> 00:49:40,714
(Another handful...)

1250
00:49:40,714 --> 00:49:44,084
(so that the chickens can enjoy it to their hearts' content)

1251
00:49:44,354 --> 00:49:46,724
(After all that cutting,)

1252
00:49:47,524 --> 00:49:50,554
(the cart is piled high with grass.)

1253
00:49:50,994 --> 00:49:53,164
(Now it's time to feed the chickens.)

1254
00:49:53,724 --> 00:49:55,124
(Following)

1255
00:49:55,124 --> 00:49:56,564
Oh, my. I guess the chickens know...

1256
00:49:56,564 --> 00:49:57,594
- it's snack time.
- Come this way.

1257
00:49:58,164 --> 00:49:59,364
They know it's snack time.

1258
00:49:59,364 --> 00:50:01,034
(Having heard the news, the customers gather.)

1259
00:50:01,464 --> 00:50:03,634
(Snacks!)

1260
00:50:05,174 --> 00:50:08,704
(Hearing the news, the chickens line up even before the grass arrives.)

1261
00:50:12,074 --> 00:50:14,614
- Get out of the way. Move.
- Come on.

1262
00:50:15,084 --> 00:50:17,484
It's dangerous.

1263
00:50:17,484 --> 00:50:18,484
(Running)

1264
00:50:18,484 --> 00:50:19,524
It's dangerous.

1265
00:50:19,524 --> 00:50:23,154
(A flock of chickens comes flocking in like a cloud.)

1266
00:50:23,154 --> 00:50:24,994
- Okay. Place it there.
- Wait.

1267
00:50:25,594 --> 00:50:26,594
Place some around.

1268
00:50:27,394 --> 00:50:28,524
(Got a big piece)

1269
00:50:30,864 --> 00:50:31,964
- Look at these guys.
- How cute!

1270
00:50:33,634 --> 00:50:36,204
(The chickens are munching away.)

1271
00:50:37,674 --> 00:50:39,344
(Seeing them dig in makes them happy)

1272
00:50:41,174 --> 00:50:44,174
(The snack lady is hard at work.)

1273
00:50:44,414 --> 00:50:45,644
This is really amusing.

1274
00:50:45,814 --> 00:50:46,844
Dig in.

1275
00:50:47,984 --> 00:50:49,014
How cute.

1276
00:50:50,914 --> 00:50:51,984
Enjoy, okay?

1277
00:50:51,984 --> 00:50:53,024
Come this way.

1278
00:50:53,524 --> 00:50:55,254
(Thanks for the food!)

1279
00:50:55,254 --> 00:50:56,994
Give me a second. Let's see.

1280
00:50:56,994 --> 00:50:58,094
I'm sorry.

1281
00:50:58,094 --> 00:50:59,694
(Not a single foot of space to spare)

1282
00:51:00,324 --> 00:51:01,694
The crowd is making things hard.

1283
00:51:01,924 --> 00:51:02,934
Give me a little space.

1284
00:51:04,294 --> 00:51:05,564
The grass is over here, guys.

1285
00:51:05,564 --> 00:51:07,004
Come here, not there.

1286
00:51:07,004 --> 00:51:08,004
(Grass Yoon Seo scattered)

1287
00:51:08,234 --> 00:51:09,234
There's a bunch here.

1288
00:51:09,234 --> 00:51:10,974
(The customers are gathered in a different spot.)

1289
00:51:11,104 --> 00:51:12,374
Come over here.

1290
00:51:12,974 --> 00:51:14,004
- Here's some grass.
- Food.

1291
00:51:14,174 --> 00:51:15,244
Follow me.

1292
00:51:15,444 --> 00:51:16,674
Will they eat if I serve it to them?

1293
00:51:16,674 --> 00:51:18,714
Come over here.

1294
00:51:18,984 --> 00:51:19,984
Here. Dig in.

1295
00:51:19,984 --> 00:51:21,214
(It's yummy grass!)

1296
00:51:21,744 --> 00:51:24,014
(Eating the fresh grass)

1297
00:51:25,054 --> 00:51:26,254
They look cute.

1298
00:51:26,684 --> 00:51:28,084
- What?
- They look cute,

1299
00:51:28,084 --> 00:51:29,224
- They sure dig in.
- looking closely.

1300
00:51:30,524 --> 00:51:31,594
I thought I'd be scared of them.

1301
00:51:31,594 --> 00:51:32,824
(Being charmed by the chickens while feeding them)

1302
00:51:33,324 --> 00:51:34,394
They're enjoying it.

1303
00:51:36,134 --> 00:51:38,494
- Dig in! Enjoy!
- Dig in!

1304
00:51:38,494 --> 00:51:39,564
Enjoy!

1305
00:51:39,564 --> 00:51:41,534
(Done feeding the chickens grass)

1306
00:51:41,534 --> 00:51:43,074
- We'll be collecting eggs.
- Okay.

1307
00:51:43,074 --> 00:51:44,104
I'm leaving.

1308
00:51:44,204 --> 00:51:46,144
When collecting eggs,

1309
00:51:46,804 --> 00:51:48,174
try not to talk.

1310
00:51:48,174 --> 00:51:49,544
- Speak softly.
- Okay.

1311
00:51:49,544 --> 00:51:52,584
Place the big eggs around the cart...

1312
00:51:52,584 --> 00:51:55,184
- and small eggs in the center.
- The center?

1313
00:51:55,384 --> 00:51:57,154
The pointy end should face down.

1314
00:51:57,154 --> 00:51:58,254
Down.

1315
00:51:58,254 --> 00:51:59,424
(Place the eggs pointy end down.)

1316
00:51:59,954 --> 00:52:02,024
(There's an air pocket at the rounded end, so storing eggs...)

1317
00:52:02,024 --> 00:52:03,924
(with the pointed end down helps keep them fresh.)

1318
00:52:04,054 --> 00:52:05,394
(Eggs will be collected from three complexes today.)

1319
00:52:05,394 --> 00:52:07,224
(Complexes 1, 2, 3)

1320
00:52:08,124 --> 00:52:09,764
- Follow me.
- Okay.

1321
00:52:10,534 --> 00:52:12,304
Try not to talk, if possible.

1322
00:52:12,304 --> 00:52:14,134
The chickens are waiting to lay eggs...

1323
00:52:14,134 --> 00:52:16,304
- right now.
- I see.

1324
00:52:16,574 --> 00:52:18,304
- This way.
- They're giving birth right now.

1325
00:52:18,634 --> 00:52:21,044
I'll talk very softly.

1326
00:52:21,944 --> 00:52:23,074
This way.

1327
00:52:23,074 --> 00:52:24,544
(Entering the henhouse to collect fresh eggs)

1328
00:52:24,544 --> 00:52:26,114
Let me show you.

1329
00:52:27,614 --> 00:52:30,284
(Slowly reaching in so the chickens don't get startled)

1330
00:52:30,284 --> 00:52:33,924
If you push in very slowly, it's okay.

1331
00:52:34,884 --> 00:52:38,494
(Gently take the eggs out, and that's it.)

1332
00:52:38,794 --> 00:52:46,794
(Most importantly, make sure not to startle the chickens.)

1333
00:52:48,604 --> 00:52:51,234
It just laid this one. It's a freshly laid egg.

1334
00:52:51,934 --> 00:52:52,944
(Secured freshly laid eggs)

1335
00:52:52,944 --> 00:52:53,944
- Like this.
- A freshly laid egg.

1336
00:52:54,444 --> 00:52:55,844
Excuse me.

1337
00:52:55,844 --> 00:52:59,184
You have to place your hand inside and grab the egg out.

1338
00:52:59,184 --> 00:53:00,384
(Flying off)

1339
00:53:00,644 --> 00:53:01,814
(Screaming)

1340
00:53:01,814 --> 00:53:02,984
I'm sorry.

1341
00:53:03,414 --> 00:53:05,114
(I had to be quiet, but I couldn't.)

1342
00:53:05,114 --> 00:53:06,154
I'm sorry.

1343
00:53:06,584 --> 00:53:08,124
Try placing your hand inside.

1344
00:53:08,124 --> 00:53:09,194
(Trying again)

1345
00:53:09,194 --> 00:53:11,124
Check if there are any eggs.

1346
00:53:11,124 --> 00:53:12,294
- Are there?
- It's warm.

1347
00:53:14,094 --> 00:53:15,664
That's it. That's how you do it.

1348
00:53:15,664 --> 00:53:16,664
(She successfully collected her first eggs!)

1349
00:53:16,664 --> 00:53:17,764
Just like that.

1350
00:53:19,804 --> 00:53:21,734
(This time, Yoon Seo tries alone.)

1351
00:53:22,234 --> 00:53:24,174
(Touching)

1352
00:53:24,174 --> 00:53:26,444
There are three in here. I'm sorry. Excuse me for a bit.

1353
00:53:28,244 --> 00:53:30,074
(Collected 3 eggs in 1 go)

1354
00:53:30,814 --> 00:53:32,044
The pointy end down.

1355
00:53:33,914 --> 00:53:35,614
(Meanwhile, how's Jung Ah doing?)

1356
00:53:36,214 --> 00:53:39,184
(Hesitating)

1357
00:53:40,124 --> 00:53:42,124
(Jung Ah has always been scared of animals.)

1358
00:53:42,524 --> 00:53:44,494
(Staring)

1359
00:53:46,224 --> 00:53:47,924
(Confronting it without reaching in)

1360
00:53:48,464 --> 00:53:50,934
(She spotted an empty nest.)

1361
00:53:50,994 --> 00:53:52,704
(After reading the chicken's face,)

1362
00:53:53,434 --> 00:53:56,304
(she quickly gets one egg while the chicken is gone.)

1363
00:53:56,674 --> 00:53:58,974
(Jung Ah contributed by adding an egg.)

1364
00:53:59,774 --> 00:54:01,244
She can't do it.

1365
00:54:02,414 --> 00:54:04,344
- I can't lift it up.
- No.

1366
00:54:05,344 --> 00:54:07,314
I can't put my hand inside.

1367
00:54:07,344 --> 00:54:08,484
- You can't?
- No.

1368
00:54:11,284 --> 00:54:12,354
Right here.

1369
00:54:12,354 --> 00:54:13,354
(Spotted an empty nest)

1370
00:54:13,354 --> 00:54:14,354
Only the visible ones.

1371
00:54:14,354 --> 00:54:15,994
- Only the visible ones.
- Yes.

1372
00:54:17,124 --> 00:54:22,894
(Jung Ah targets the nests that are empty.)

1373
00:54:23,164 --> 00:54:25,134
There's a bunch here. After laying them...

1374
00:54:25,134 --> 00:54:26,934
(Did the chicken go somewhere?)

1375
00:54:27,604 --> 00:54:28,834
How kind of it.

1376
00:54:28,834 --> 00:54:29,834
(Collecting the eggs while the chicken is gone)

1377
00:54:32,844 --> 00:54:35,204
(Filled up a carton by collecting eggs from empty nests)

1378
00:54:36,314 --> 00:54:37,344
I'm sorry.

1379
00:54:38,314 --> 00:54:39,344
Okay.

1380
00:54:40,184 --> 00:54:41,484
(Feeling bad about collecting the eggs)

1381
00:54:41,484 --> 00:54:42,514
I'm sorry.

1382
00:54:44,184 --> 00:54:47,084
(Yoon Seo is being gentle so as not to scare the chicken.)

1383
00:54:47,524 --> 00:54:49,654
(My eggs...)

1384
00:54:49,824 --> 00:54:51,254
It's giving birth right now.

1385
00:54:52,864 --> 00:54:53,994
I should be careful.

1386
00:54:57,064 --> 00:54:58,234
Put the pointed end down.

1387
00:55:00,204 --> 00:55:01,264
(Clucking)

1388
00:55:01,264 --> 00:55:02,334
(Startled)

1389
00:55:03,134 --> 00:55:04,134
(Clucking)

1390
00:55:04,134 --> 00:55:05,744
That scared me. Gosh.

1391
00:55:07,444 --> 00:55:08,444
(1 egg)

1392
00:55:08,444 --> 00:55:09,574
It might peck at me.

1393
00:55:09,574 --> 00:55:10,714
(Scared but continuously working)

1394
00:55:10,714 --> 00:55:11,844
There are three here.

1395
00:55:12,884 --> 00:55:13,884
(3 eggs)

1396
00:55:14,044 --> 00:55:15,114
Hold on.

1397
00:55:15,584 --> 00:55:16,684
You're doing well.

1398
00:55:17,054 --> 00:55:18,184
It's your calling.

1399
00:55:18,484 --> 00:55:19,554
- Really?
- Yes.

1400
00:55:19,984 --> 00:55:20,984
All right.

1401
00:55:21,224 --> 00:55:22,254
Did you collect a lot, Jung Ah?

1402
00:55:22,254 --> 00:55:24,224
I only need one more egg to fill a carton.

1403
00:55:24,854 --> 00:55:27,324
(Moving to the next complex while pulling the egg cart)

1404
00:55:27,324 --> 00:55:28,394
Pardon me.

1405
00:55:30,094 --> 00:55:31,094
That's it.

1406
00:55:32,534 --> 00:55:33,534
Well done.

1407
00:55:34,304 --> 00:55:35,434
Excuse me.

1408
00:55:35,634 --> 00:55:38,934
(She even collects the eggs the chickens are brooding.)

1409
00:55:39,344 --> 00:55:40,344
(3 eggs)

1410
00:55:41,374 --> 00:55:42,404
(Being careful)

1411
00:55:42,404 --> 00:55:43,474
I'm sorry.

1412
00:55:45,714 --> 00:55:47,514
Gosh, four eggs? You laid a lot.

1413
00:55:47,944 --> 00:55:49,044
There are five!

1414
00:55:49,514 --> 00:55:54,124
(Found an egg bonanza)

1415
00:55:54,954 --> 00:55:56,954
(Already quite skilled with her hands)

1416
00:55:56,954 --> 00:55:58,054
This one's slightly small.

1417
00:55:58,824 --> 00:56:00,994
(Jung Ah is trying again.)

1418
00:56:02,494 --> 00:56:03,494
(Startled)

1419
00:56:03,634 --> 00:56:06,704
(Collecting the egg quickly while the chicken is away)

1420
00:56:06,934 --> 00:56:08,634
(Checking out the next empty nest)

1421
00:56:09,374 --> 00:56:11,104
(It looked like an empty nest, but the owner appeared.)

1422
00:56:12,174 --> 00:56:14,344
(But she's still targeting empty nests.)

1423
00:56:14,344 --> 00:56:15,504
Quickly.

1424
00:56:17,544 --> 00:56:20,284
(Knowing how Jung Ah feels, the chicken makes way.)

1425
00:56:21,414 --> 00:56:24,514
(Frozen)

1426
00:56:24,854 --> 00:56:25,954
Oh, my gosh.

1427
00:56:26,424 --> 00:56:27,554
It's far inside.

1428
00:56:28,384 --> 00:56:29,824
(The owner is inside the nest.)

1429
00:56:30,954 --> 00:56:33,694
(She reaches for the egg while holding her breath.)

1430
00:56:34,424 --> 00:56:35,724
(Anxious)

1431
00:56:36,694 --> 00:56:37,694
(Collected only an egg)

1432
00:56:37,694 --> 00:56:38,764
(Breathing out)

1433
00:56:38,764 --> 00:56:40,864
(Current time: 10am)

1434
00:56:41,164 --> 00:56:43,174
(Team Home hasn't even started cooking.)

1435
00:56:43,804 --> 00:56:44,804
Gosh.

1436
00:56:45,404 --> 00:56:46,674
What are you doing, Sun Young?

1437
00:56:46,674 --> 00:56:48,504
- What?
- What are you doing?

1438
00:56:48,974 --> 00:56:51,314
- Welcome back.
- Thanks.

1439
00:56:52,514 --> 00:56:54,784
(Can they really be taking their time?)

1440
00:56:55,144 --> 00:56:56,354
I don't know what I'll make,

1441
00:56:56,354 --> 00:56:57,914
but let's get to it now.

1442
00:56:58,384 --> 00:56:59,424
Let's go.

1443
00:57:00,024 --> 00:57:01,324
Let's go.

1444
00:57:02,654 --> 00:57:05,724
I must make breakfast without Jung Ah today.

1445
00:57:07,094 --> 00:57:09,534
(Raised in Taean's pristine tidal flats)

1446
00:57:10,394 --> 00:57:13,904
(The second dish made with the plump, chewy clams)

1447
00:57:14,264 --> 00:57:15,534
- For the soft tofu stew, - Yes?

1448
00:57:15,534 --> 00:57:16,834
it only takes 20 minutes to cook.

1449
00:57:18,434 --> 00:57:20,644
(And with the eggs collected by Jung Ah and Yoon Seo)

1450
00:57:20,774 --> 00:57:22,204
Next, rolled omelet.

1451
00:57:22,204 --> 00:57:24,114
What were we going to make? Soft tofu stew. Rolled omelet.

1452
00:57:24,674 --> 00:57:25,714
(You Seok and Sun Young's to-do list)

1453
00:57:25,714 --> 00:57:26,714
(Cook rice, prep ingredients for rolled omelet,)

1454
00:57:26,714 --> 00:57:27,744
(cook Manila clam soft tofu stew)

1455
00:57:27,844 --> 00:57:29,014
I'd better cut up the vegetables...

1456
00:57:29,014 --> 00:57:31,684
for the rolled omelet right now, right?

1457
00:57:32,084 --> 00:57:34,654
Okay, I'll finely chop the vegetables for the rolled omelet.

1458
00:57:34,654 --> 00:57:36,194
(The first ingredient prep without Jung Ah)

1459
00:57:37,354 --> 00:57:38,554
Vegetables.

1460
00:57:39,524 --> 00:57:40,764
Onions.

1461
00:57:41,764 --> 00:57:44,594
Do we add chilli to the rolled omelet?

1462
00:57:44,964 --> 00:57:46,134
(Do we add chilli...)

1463
00:57:46,604 --> 00:57:47,764
(to the rolled omelet?)

1464
00:57:50,774 --> 00:57:52,004
Chilli is too spicy.

1465
00:57:52,674 --> 00:57:53,874
Let's not put it in.

1466
00:57:54,944 --> 00:57:57,314
(Who is she talking to?)

1467
00:57:57,544 --> 00:57:58,574
Green onions and...

1468
00:57:59,384 --> 00:58:00,484
(Green onions?)

1469
00:58:01,084 --> 00:58:03,814
Should I chop up these green onions for the rolled omelet...

1470
00:58:03,814 --> 00:58:05,884
or spring onions that are thinner?

1471
00:58:07,824 --> 00:58:09,084
Okay, let's use spring onions.

1472
00:58:09,494 --> 00:58:11,754
(She once again solves the question by answering it herself.)

1473
00:58:12,124 --> 00:58:13,124
Spring onions.

1474
00:58:13,524 --> 00:58:15,494
Carrots. Carrots are a must.

1475
00:58:16,564 --> 00:58:17,594
Okay.

1476
00:58:17,594 --> 00:58:19,504
(Let's get to washing the ingredients.)

1477
00:58:20,704 --> 00:58:23,034
(Washing the dirty roots of the spring onions first)

1478
00:58:23,034 --> 00:58:25,234
Do I throw this part out or what?

1479
00:58:25,234 --> 00:58:26,944
What am I supposed to do?

1480
00:58:28,204 --> 00:58:29,614
This part is inedible. Throw it out.

1481
00:58:31,474 --> 00:58:32,744
Or is it an important part?

1482
00:58:35,114 --> 00:58:38,214
(It's actually the most nutritious part.)

1483
00:58:38,814 --> 00:58:42,054
(Sun Young just cuts it off.)

1484
00:58:42,794 --> 00:58:44,054
(She moves on to the onion next.)

1485
00:58:44,054 --> 00:58:45,194
We'd better cook rice.

1486
00:58:45,724 --> 00:58:47,264
(While peeling the onion,)

1487
00:58:48,294 --> 00:58:50,794
(she even cuts the normal parts.)

1488
00:58:51,734 --> 00:58:54,734
(A cooking novice awkwardly prepping vegetables)

1489
00:58:55,504 --> 00:58:58,334
(While Sun Young is prepping the ingredients and making huge losses)

1490
00:58:58,974 --> 00:58:59,974
Okay.

1491
00:58:59,974 --> 00:59:01,104
(Before cooking the soft tofu stew,)

1492
00:59:01,104 --> 00:59:02,144
(You Seok starts with the rice.)

1493
00:59:03,244 --> 00:59:04,274
Rice...

1494
00:59:06,014 --> 00:59:07,584
One cup is one portion.

1495
00:59:08,384 --> 00:59:10,014
We have four in total.

1496
00:59:10,014 --> 00:59:11,654
(He can easily cook rice.)

1497
00:59:11,654 --> 00:59:12,854
I should cook at least three portions.

1498
00:59:13,954 --> 00:59:16,254
(Since Jung Ah and Yoon Seo would've worked hard)

1499
00:59:17,094 --> 00:59:19,494
Let's add a little black rice and make black rice.

1500
00:59:21,324 --> 00:59:24,334
(You Seok brings it over to the sink.)

1501
00:59:24,994 --> 00:59:27,304
(Like a pro home cook,)

1502
00:59:27,304 --> 00:59:29,434
(he's skilled at washing the rice.)

1503
00:59:29,434 --> 00:59:31,474
(You Seok didn't waste a single grain of rice.)

1504
00:59:32,504 --> 00:59:35,704
(After eyeballing the amount of water)

1505
00:59:36,974 --> 00:59:37,974
(Slightly)

1506
00:59:38,444 --> 00:59:39,444
(Adding slightly more)

1507
00:59:40,514 --> 00:59:42,644
(Checking it for the last time on a flat surface)

1508
00:59:42,644 --> 00:59:43,854
(Satisfied)

1509
00:59:44,814 --> 00:59:48,384
(A pro home cook with serious solo-living skills)

1510
00:59:48,684 --> 00:59:51,254
Shall we get started? The vegetables.

1511
00:59:52,324 --> 00:59:55,264
Chopping these up is easy peasy.

1512
00:59:56,094 --> 00:59:57,334
(Chopping up the spring onions fast)

1513
00:59:57,334 --> 00:59:59,664
This size should be fine, right? About this size.

1514
00:59:59,664 --> 01:00:00,904
(These are not chives.)

1515
01:00:01,164 --> 01:00:02,204
This much should do.

1516
01:00:02,704 --> 01:00:03,874
Add in the spring onions.

1517
01:00:04,304 --> 01:00:05,534
Next, the onion.

1518
01:00:05,534 --> 01:00:07,274
(Moving on straight to the onion)

1519
01:00:07,274 --> 01:00:08,304
Onion.

1520
01:00:08,374 --> 01:00:10,714
I'd better chop it pretty. Jung Ah likes it pretty.

1521
01:00:12,514 --> 01:00:15,944
(Sun Young chops the onion finely and neatly.)

1522
01:00:16,554 --> 01:00:19,084
Like this, so that it turns out square.

1523
01:00:20,154 --> 01:00:22,184
(This doesn't look right.)

1524
01:00:22,424 --> 01:00:23,454
The onion...

1525
01:00:24,224 --> 01:00:26,224
will turn sweet when cooked,

1526
01:00:26,224 --> 01:00:28,094
so even if it's thick, it's easy to eat.

1527
01:00:29,024 --> 01:00:30,764
The onion looks too thick, though.

1528
01:00:32,234 --> 01:00:35,234
It's okay. The onion doesn't have to be cooked fully.

1529
01:00:36,734 --> 01:00:38,534
Next, the carrot.

1530
01:00:39,904 --> 01:00:42,174
Those back from work might not be pleased...

1531
01:00:42,274 --> 01:00:44,544
if they chew on carrots while eating the egg omelet.

1532
01:00:45,544 --> 01:00:46,614
I'll chop them finely.

1533
01:00:46,614 --> 01:00:49,344
(Sun Young basically minces the carrot.)

1534
01:00:49,884 --> 01:00:53,024
(But it's still big.)

1535
01:00:53,384 --> 01:00:54,654
Okay, all minced.

1536
01:00:54,784 --> 01:00:55,954
(Sun Young is quite pleased with it.)

1537
01:00:55,954 --> 01:00:57,694
Okay. The more carrots, the tastier.

1538
01:00:57,724 --> 01:00:58,794
All done.

1539
01:00:58,794 --> 01:00:59,864
(You Seok and Sun Young's to-do list)

1540
01:00:59,864 --> 01:01:00,924
(Cook Manila clam soft tofu stew)

1541
01:01:01,594 --> 01:01:03,534
(Meanwhile, did Jung Ah find another empty nest?)

1542
01:01:04,334 --> 01:01:08,504
(It's a nest with a chicken brooding on the egg!)

1543
01:01:08,964 --> 01:01:11,634
(Where did Jung Ah, who only went for empty nests, go?)

1544
01:01:14,744 --> 01:01:19,814
(Collecting eggs without any hesitation whatsoever now)

1545
01:01:21,484 --> 01:01:25,354
(Jung Ah has grown more confident in taking the eggs out.)

1546
01:01:25,354 --> 01:01:26,354
(1 egg)

1547
01:01:30,094 --> 01:01:31,094
(1 egg)

1548
01:01:34,964 --> 01:01:37,464
The egg is warm because the chicken just laid it.

1549
01:01:38,564 --> 01:01:39,604
(Clucking)

1550
01:01:44,104 --> 01:01:45,834
(Jung Ah has become comfortable to the point of...)

1551
01:01:45,834 --> 01:01:47,704
(collecting eggs that the chickens are brooding.)

1552
01:01:47,974 --> 01:01:50,444
(Thoughtfully moving away)

1553
01:01:51,374 --> 01:01:52,374
(3 eggs)

1554
01:01:53,014 --> 01:01:54,114
(Thanks to it, Jung Ah collects the egg easily.)

1555
01:01:54,114 --> 01:01:55,144
Just one.

1556
01:01:58,714 --> 01:01:59,984
(Even moving away for Yoon Seo)

1557
01:02:02,184 --> 01:02:05,694
(There are a whopping 5 eggs!)

1558
01:02:07,224 --> 01:02:09,734
It's a party of eggs!

1559
01:02:11,164 --> 01:02:12,264
- All done.
- Yes.

1560
01:02:12,764 --> 01:02:14,404
They must know we're here for the eggs.

1561
01:02:14,864 --> 01:02:16,734
- The chickens?
- Yes, they stay still.

1562
01:02:19,374 --> 01:02:20,644
Let's gather them.

1563
01:02:21,574 --> 01:02:23,174
(However, the eggs are different in size.)

1564
01:02:23,174 --> 01:02:24,444
Are they classified as extra-large...

1565
01:02:24,444 --> 01:02:26,044
- or large based on their size?
- Yes.

1566
01:02:26,044 --> 01:02:27,944
But we don't classify them as much.

1567
01:02:28,114 --> 01:02:29,884
- See how the colours are different?
- Yes.

1568
01:02:29,884 --> 01:02:31,014
The colours are what matter.

1569
01:02:33,354 --> 01:02:35,854
Depending on what they are fed,

1570
01:02:35,854 --> 01:02:37,294
the yolk's colour changes.

1571
01:02:38,054 --> 01:02:40,064
So it changes depending on...

1572
01:02:40,064 --> 01:02:41,364
what the chickens eat.

1573
01:02:41,364 --> 01:02:43,034
- The colours are all different.
- Yes.

1574
01:02:43,034 --> 01:02:44,334
- It's a marker.
- This is what makes the egg...

1575
01:02:44,334 --> 01:02:45,634
free-range, number one.

1576
01:02:45,634 --> 01:02:46,634
Original eggs.

1577
01:02:46,634 --> 01:02:47,704
In short,

1578
01:02:47,704 --> 01:02:49,334
- the diverse colours are best.
- Exactly.

1579
01:02:50,104 --> 01:02:51,334
That's a useful tip.

1580
01:02:51,334 --> 01:02:53,104
Place yours on top. You collected more.

1581
01:02:54,244 --> 01:02:55,304
I'll pull it.

1582
01:02:58,974 --> 01:03:00,744
(Bye!)

1583
01:03:00,884 --> 01:03:01,914
Bye.

1584
01:03:01,914 --> 01:03:03,114
(Bye, chickens! Thanks for the eggs!)

1585
01:03:04,214 --> 01:03:05,284
They're cute.

1586
01:03:05,284 --> 01:03:06,284
Thank you.

1587
01:03:06,284 --> 01:03:09,124
(How many did the two collect?)

1588
01:03:10,154 --> 01:03:12,354
- One, two, three, - Yes.

1589
01:03:12,794 --> 01:03:13,864
four, five. Five cartons.

1590
01:03:13,864 --> 01:03:15,294
- Five cartons.
- Five cartons of eggs.

1591
01:03:16,594 --> 01:03:18,794
(The eggs collected by Jung Ah and Yoon Seo are...)

1592
01:03:19,834 --> 01:03:22,004
(placed on the machine with an adhesion device,)

1593
01:03:22,304 --> 01:03:29,204
(cleaned thoroughly, sorted out,)

1594
01:03:29,944 --> 01:03:31,774
(packed nicely in cartons, and delivered directly nationwide.)

1595
01:03:35,514 --> 01:03:37,084
Good work today.

1596
01:03:37,084 --> 01:03:38,154
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1597
01:03:39,924 --> 01:03:40,954
But...

1598
01:03:41,284 --> 01:03:42,284
- Really?
- Yes.

1599
01:03:42,284 --> 01:03:44,554
- Take these and enjoy them.
- They look really fresh.

1600
01:03:44,554 --> 01:03:46,054
Look how clean they are.

1601
01:03:46,494 --> 01:03:47,564
Thank you so much.

1602
01:03:47,824 --> 01:03:49,164
Let's have one each.

1603
01:03:49,564 --> 01:03:50,794
- This? Raw egg?
- Yes.

1604
01:03:50,794 --> 01:03:52,564
- Go ahead, if you'd like.
- You see,

1605
01:03:52,564 --> 01:03:53,664
I've never tried it before.

1606
01:03:53,664 --> 01:03:54,664
- Never?
- No.

1607
01:03:54,664 --> 01:03:56,164
- Me neither. Does it smell?
- First...

1608
01:03:56,164 --> 01:03:58,334
No. We're told our eggs don't smell,

1609
01:03:58,334 --> 01:04:00,574
but I personally don't eat raw eggs.

1610
01:04:00,574 --> 01:04:02,074
- But those who eat them...
- Why...

1611
01:04:02,204 --> 01:04:03,514
Why do you not eat them raw?

1612
01:04:03,514 --> 01:04:05,014
I can't because I'm squeamish.

1613
01:04:05,474 --> 01:04:06,884
Same here.

1614
01:04:06,884 --> 01:04:08,144
I'm not having one.

1615
01:04:08,814 --> 01:04:09,914
I've never tried it.

1616
01:04:10,514 --> 01:04:13,084
I like my eggs half-cooked.

1617
01:04:13,484 --> 01:04:14,654
- Half-cooked eggs are good.
- Right?

1618
01:04:15,354 --> 01:04:16,694
I heard it was flavourful.

1619
01:04:17,054 --> 01:04:18,394
- You heard from others?
- Yes.

1620
01:04:18,924 --> 01:04:20,994
This one is good. It was freshly laid.

1621
01:04:21,264 --> 01:04:22,564
But you've never tried one either.

1622
01:04:22,564 --> 01:04:24,894
Come on, it's for you.

1623
01:04:25,594 --> 01:04:27,564
- Do I...
- I blocked this side, okay?

1624
01:04:27,804 --> 01:04:28,834
Okay.

1625
01:04:29,064 --> 01:04:31,574
Drink it. Suck it out.

1626
01:04:33,174 --> 01:04:34,204
Oh, my.

1627
01:04:34,504 --> 01:04:37,074
(Yoon Seo is trying her very first raw egg.)

1628
01:04:39,344 --> 01:04:41,314
The taste is gone quickly, but it was savoury.

1629
01:04:42,314 --> 01:04:43,314
It was savoury.

1630
01:04:43,984 --> 01:04:45,314
- It's savoury.
- Yes.

1631
01:04:46,184 --> 01:04:47,984
I was surprised because it was a lot.

1632
01:04:48,254 --> 01:04:49,754
- I gave you a small one.
- It hits you hard.

1633
01:04:49,754 --> 01:04:51,454
Yes. That's why I was frowning.

1634
01:04:51,454 --> 01:04:52,524
(Laughing)

1635
01:04:52,794 --> 01:04:53,794
Thank you.

1636
01:04:55,124 --> 01:04:56,834
Good job.

1637
01:04:56,934 --> 01:04:59,364
Take it and enjoy it. You must be hungry.

1638
01:04:59,364 --> 01:05:01,464
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1639
01:05:01,464 --> 01:05:02,604
- Thank you.
- Such precious eggs.

1640
01:05:02,934 --> 01:05:05,704
My throat is...

1641
01:05:06,174 --> 01:05:09,174
- Like lubricant... I should sing.
- You should sing.

1642
01:05:09,404 --> 01:05:12,174
- It'll make you sing.
- It's so smooth.

1643
01:05:13,284 --> 01:05:14,944
This much first. It's bothersome.

1644
01:05:16,214 --> 01:05:17,914
You better hurry.

1645
01:05:17,914 --> 01:05:19,684
Are they done?

1646
01:05:20,654 --> 01:05:23,654
Really? Is Jung Ah on the way?

1647
01:05:24,054 --> 01:05:25,854
(Suddenly hit with the bad news)

1648
01:05:25,854 --> 01:05:26,894
What?

1649
01:05:27,094 --> 01:05:29,164
(What they have ready so far...)

1650
01:05:29,664 --> 01:05:32,464
(is purple rice.)

1651
01:05:33,234 --> 01:05:35,434
(He leisurely went for a run...)

1652
01:05:36,134 --> 01:05:38,234
(and she leisurely put on makeup.)

1653
01:05:38,534 --> 01:05:41,644
You Seok, make soft tofu stew now.

1654
01:05:41,974 --> 01:05:44,214
The rolled omelet can be done real quick.

1655
01:05:44,874 --> 01:05:45,914
(He quickly takes the ingredients.)

1656
01:05:45,914 --> 01:05:46,944
Boil soft tofu.

1657
01:05:48,044 --> 01:05:50,484
(Running to the yard)

1658
01:05:51,384 --> 01:05:53,084
(The two grasshoppers are under the gun.)

1659
01:05:53,084 --> 01:05:54,984
- Are you going to cut them?
- Yes, I'll be quick.

1660
01:05:56,594 --> 01:05:57,624
They just left.

1661
01:05:57,624 --> 01:05:58,624
(He's in a hurry.)

1662
01:05:58,624 --> 01:05:59,694
Let's hurry up.

1663
01:06:01,394 --> 01:06:04,594
(Sun Young shuts her mouth and cuts the ingredients too.)

1664
01:06:05,234 --> 01:06:08,504
(Cutting super fast)

1665
01:06:08,964 --> 01:06:11,034
(They barely manage to prepare the ingredients.)

1666
01:06:11,974 --> 01:06:15,574
(All they need to do now is to stir-fry and boil them.)

1667
01:06:16,274 --> 01:06:17,844
(Picking up)

1668
01:06:18,444 --> 01:06:21,414
(There's no time for a break. He starts cooking immediately.)

1669
01:06:22,314 --> 01:06:25,054
(Here's how fast a home-cooked food master can go.)

1670
01:06:25,684 --> 01:06:26,954
(Apply oil on the pan first.)

1671
01:06:26,954 --> 01:06:28,424
You need to stir-fry green onions first.

1672
01:06:29,124 --> 01:06:31,024
You're making green onion oil? That's cool.

1673
01:06:32,994 --> 01:06:36,294
(Throwing in green onions)

1674
01:06:36,764 --> 01:06:39,064
(Flashy wrist snaps)

1675
01:06:39,834 --> 01:06:41,234
(Glancing)

1676
01:06:41,734 --> 01:06:44,404
You're good at cooking, You Seok.

1677
01:06:45,174 --> 01:06:46,944
(This is me.)

1678
01:06:47,374 --> 01:06:49,744
(You Seok looks like a master chef.)

1679
01:06:50,574 --> 01:06:52,814
(Adding chilli powder)

1680
01:06:53,444 --> 01:06:55,214
Green onion oil and chilli oil.

1681
01:06:55,214 --> 01:06:56,584
(Stir-fry it quickly with green onions.)

1682
01:06:57,154 --> 01:06:59,454
(Green onion and chilli oil for Manila clam soft tofu stew)

1683
01:06:59,884 --> 01:07:01,954
- I'm done.
- You're done?

1684
01:07:01,954 --> 01:07:03,054
- I'm done.
- Okay.

1685
01:07:03,354 --> 01:07:04,424
I'm done.

1686
01:07:04,424 --> 01:07:05,494
(They can finish cooking before Jung Ah arrives.)

1687
01:07:06,524 --> 01:07:08,624
(He just needs to stir-fry onions before adding water.)

1688
01:07:10,764 --> 01:07:13,404
What?

1689
01:07:13,864 --> 01:07:15,434
- They're here. This is bad.
- Where?

1690
01:07:15,934 --> 01:07:18,774
(Team Poultry Farm has already arrived?)

1691
01:07:20,644 --> 01:07:22,874
Did they prepare the food?

1692
01:07:24,014 --> 01:07:25,114
Will it not be ready?

1693
01:07:26,714 --> 01:07:29,044
(Hungry Jung Ah is approaching.)

1694
01:07:29,344 --> 01:07:31,984
(But none of the dishes are ready.)

1695
01:07:32,284 --> 01:07:34,524
I shouldn't be doing this.

1696
01:07:35,624 --> 01:07:36,724
Do I cook rolled omelet there?

1697
01:07:36,724 --> 01:07:38,854
(Jung Ah arrives earlier than they thought.)

1698
01:07:38,854 --> 01:07:39,864
Is the rice ready?

1699
01:07:39,864 --> 01:07:41,324
(Panicked)

1700
01:07:42,524 --> 01:07:43,594
Hold on.

1701
01:07:44,364 --> 01:07:45,364
A big wok...

1702
01:07:45,934 --> 01:07:48,064
Wait, I don't need this.

1703
01:07:48,364 --> 01:07:49,904
This... Go back.

1704
01:07:50,874 --> 01:07:54,404
I want to eat soft tofu stew as soon as I arrive.

1705
01:07:55,474 --> 01:07:57,374
(Jung Ah arriving in 20 seconds)

1706
01:07:58,014 --> 01:08:00,144
(You Seok tries to finish it somehow.)

1707
01:08:00,814 --> 01:08:03,254
(He quickly stir-fries onions before she arrives.)

1708
01:08:03,814 --> 01:08:06,824
(He tries to add water at least.)

1709
01:08:07,624 --> 01:08:10,494
(Team Poultry Farm has arrived.)

1710
01:08:11,054 --> 01:08:12,054
(Gulping)

1711
01:08:12,424 --> 01:08:13,994
(What should I do?)

1712
01:08:14,824 --> 01:08:15,894
What...

1713
01:08:16,864 --> 01:08:18,764
- What are they doing?
- He's stir-frying something.

1714
01:08:19,394 --> 01:08:20,434
(Hold on...)

1715
01:08:20,434 --> 01:08:21,464
He's cooking.

1716
01:08:21,664 --> 01:08:23,804
Why does it look like...

1717
01:08:23,804 --> 01:08:25,634
he's stirring nothing with chopsticks?

1718
01:08:27,444 --> 01:08:30,374
(Jung Ah assesses the situation with a frown.)

1719
01:08:31,014 --> 01:08:33,014
(Sun Young comes out to the yard, pretending to be very busy.)

1720
01:08:33,014 --> 01:08:34,244
- Act busy.
- Act busy.

1721
01:08:34,344 --> 01:08:37,614
Jung Ah, good job. Was it very tough?

1722
01:08:37,814 --> 01:08:39,384
Was it very tough?

1723
01:08:40,084 --> 01:08:41,724
- Yes.
- Oh, dear.

1724
01:08:42,454 --> 01:08:43,554
(Sun Young and You Seok greet them as if nothing was wrong.)

1725
01:08:43,554 --> 01:08:46,124
- You're back.
- Yes. Are you done?

1726
01:08:47,294 --> 01:08:50,234
I'm done. Go and change. I'm done.

1727
01:08:50,634 --> 01:08:51,634
(Really?)

1728
01:08:51,734 --> 01:08:53,834
(She checks right away with high expectations.)

1729
01:08:57,334 --> 01:08:58,374
(Peek)

1730
01:08:58,504 --> 01:08:59,574
Is it stir-fried onion?

1731
01:09:00,144 --> 01:09:02,274
Just you wait. I'm cooking soft tofu stew.

1732
01:09:04,814 --> 01:09:07,414
(Nothing is ready for breakfast.)

1733
01:09:08,514 --> 01:09:10,214
(At the scolding that will fall upon them,)

1734
01:09:10,984 --> 01:09:14,654
(the two grasshoppers are very nervous.)

1735
01:09:15,124 --> 01:09:16,754
The vegetables are ready. That...

1736
01:09:17,354 --> 01:09:20,494
It's all ready. I'll start making rolled omelet now.

1737
01:09:21,264 --> 01:09:24,264
It's all ready. I'll start making rolled omelet now.

1738
01:09:24,264 --> 01:09:25,594
(The wasp's attack makes her confused.)

1739
01:09:26,164 --> 01:09:27,834
- Should I cut green onions?
- What?

1740
01:09:27,834 --> 01:09:29,064
- Green onions?
- We're done.

1741
01:09:29,064 --> 01:09:30,304
There's nothing for you to do.

1742
01:09:30,704 --> 01:09:33,274
Go wash your hands and get changed. You worked hard.

1743
01:09:34,204 --> 01:09:37,114
(Team Poultry Farm is sent to the room by the wasp.)

1744
01:09:37,674 --> 01:09:39,944
(Meanwhile, Sun Young and You Seok quickly prepare breakfast.)

1745
01:09:40,514 --> 01:09:41,944
I'm done. This is all.

1746
01:09:42,914 --> 01:09:44,654
(He just needs to add the seasoning and boil it.)

1747
01:09:45,354 --> 01:09:48,154
(He adds soy sauce to the stew base.)

1748
01:09:49,154 --> 01:09:54,294
(Stir-fry it until it nearly burns to increase umami.)

1749
01:09:55,064 --> 01:09:57,164
(Pouring water)

1750
01:09:58,694 --> 01:10:01,704
(It's starting to look like stew.)

1751
01:10:02,304 --> 01:10:03,834
(And the main ingredient of soft tofu stew)

1752
01:10:04,634 --> 01:10:07,904
(A generous amount of Manila clams)

1753
01:10:08,504 --> 01:10:10,344
(Boiling)

1754
01:10:11,274 --> 01:10:14,014
(Add zucchini too.)

1755
01:10:15,184 --> 01:10:19,514
(It looks perfectly like stew.)

1756
01:10:20,424 --> 01:10:22,054
(Sun Young quickly starts to make rolled omelets.)

1757
01:10:22,624 --> 01:10:23,694
Goodness.

1758
01:10:24,094 --> 01:10:26,024
I should've just gone to the poultry farm too.

1759
01:10:26,454 --> 01:10:29,124
The poultry farm looks fun.

1760
01:10:29,124 --> 01:10:30,294
(She cracks eggs while chatting.)

1761
01:10:31,264 --> 01:10:32,494
(When you crack the top notch eggs...)

1762
01:10:34,964 --> 01:10:36,264
(Bouncy)

1763
01:10:36,264 --> 01:10:38,334
The yolks are different.

1764
01:10:38,834 --> 01:10:41,274
They're fertilized eggs.

1765
01:10:41,604 --> 01:10:45,144
These are precious free-range eggs.

1766
01:10:45,744 --> 01:10:47,884
My goodness.

1767
01:10:48,244 --> 01:10:50,654
I get to eat such precious eggs.

1768
01:10:51,014 --> 01:10:52,014
I love it.

1769
01:10:53,354 --> 01:10:55,324
How many should I use?

1770
01:10:56,354 --> 01:10:59,054
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight.

1771
01:10:59,924 --> 01:11:01,064
(More?)

1772
01:11:02,364 --> 01:11:05,234
(She must be making a huge rolled omelet.)

1773
01:11:06,394 --> 01:11:07,434
(Another egg?)

1774
01:11:07,434 --> 01:11:08,504
My gosh.

1775
01:11:09,534 --> 01:11:11,774
(How big is the rolled omelet going to be?)

1776
01:11:12,534 --> 01:11:13,774
(When she adds the cut vegetables...)

1777
01:11:13,774 --> 01:11:16,174
I just need to add salt and mix it.

1778
01:11:16,644 --> 01:11:18,474
I normally don't add a lot of vegetables.

1779
01:11:18,974 --> 01:11:20,244
Because it's hard to roll.

1780
01:11:20,944 --> 01:11:22,014
Done.

1781
01:11:22,944 --> 01:11:25,884
I'll start cooking free-range eggs rolled omelet.

1782
01:11:25,884 --> 01:11:26,954
(She's excited to eat free-range eggs rolled omelet.)

1783
01:11:27,754 --> 01:11:32,654
(She starts cooking by applying oil.)

1784
01:11:33,524 --> 01:11:37,234
(She pours a generous amount onto the pan.)

1785
01:11:37,634 --> 01:11:39,094
Anything tastes good with a lot of oil.

1786
01:11:39,934 --> 01:11:41,004
You need a lot of oil.

1787
01:11:42,064 --> 01:11:44,734
