01:32:45,891 --> 01:32:47,021
Gosh. It's hot.

2298
01:32:48,091 --> 01:32:49,861
(Cheering up)

2299
01:32:49,861 --> 01:32:51,231
Okay. Shall we?

2300
01:32:51,231 --> 01:32:52,231
- Yes.
- Yes.

2301
01:32:53,301 --> 01:32:58,401
(They're off to see the sea!)

2302
01:32:58,971 --> 01:33:00,971
This is my first time seeing the sea this summer.

2303
01:33:01,711 --> 01:33:02,871
- Really?
- Yes.

2304
01:33:03,341 --> 01:33:04,671
Didn't we... That's right.

2305
01:33:04,671 --> 01:33:05,981
It's our first time going to the beach.

2306
01:33:05,981 --> 01:33:07,111
Didn't we...

2307
01:33:07,111 --> 01:33:09,651
Don't tell me we'll work when we get there.

2308
01:33:09,651 --> 01:33:10,881
Come on, Sun Young.

2309
01:33:10,881 --> 01:33:12,151
Are we not taking the photos for the posters?

2310
01:33:12,221 --> 01:33:13,821
- No way.
- That can't happen...

2311
01:33:13,821 --> 01:33:15,151
because I'm wearing slippers.

2312
01:33:15,951 --> 01:33:16,991
- Gosh.
- Goodness.

2313
01:33:16,991 --> 01:33:19,491
- What? Is that the sea or the sky?
- Gosh.

2314
01:33:19,491 --> 01:33:21,261
That's the sky. I thought it was the sea.

2315
01:33:21,961 --> 01:33:25,331
(While enjoying the amazing views around,)

2316
01:33:26,401 --> 01:33:27,801
(they drive through the dense forest.)

2317
01:33:27,801 --> 01:33:28,931
It's so pretty.

2318
01:33:31,771 --> 01:33:33,141
How did you find this spot?

2319
01:33:33,141 --> 01:33:35,171
- It's pretty.
- It's really pretty here.

2320
01:33:35,171 --> 01:33:36,411
- Gosh. The flowers are pretty too.
- Gosh.

2321
01:33:36,411 --> 01:33:37,411
Gosh. It's pretty.

2322
01:33:38,541 --> 01:33:39,581
Amazing.

2323
01:33:39,581 --> 01:33:41,541
(The beach entrance is covered with yellow flowers.)

2324
01:33:41,541 --> 01:33:42,711
Gosh. Look at the flowers.

2325
01:33:42,711 --> 01:33:43,711
(I can't believe there are flowers on the beach.)

2326
01:33:44,351 --> 01:33:48,251
(The blue sea of Taean unfolds beyond the golden tickseed.)

2327
01:33:48,251 --> 01:33:49,321
Goodness.

2328
01:33:49,921 --> 01:33:53,391
(The seemingly untouched, vast white beach...)

2329
01:33:54,261 --> 01:33:57,591
(and clear and transparent water)

2330
01:33:58,831 --> 01:34:01,971
(Taean's beautiful spot, Baengnipo Beach)

2331
01:34:02,801 --> 01:34:03,801
(With the unusual scenic view...)

2332
01:34:03,801 --> 01:34:04,871
It's pretty.

2333
01:34:06,101 --> 01:34:08,441
It's beautiful. Isn't it, Jung Ah?

2334
01:34:08,441 --> 01:34:09,541
It's so pretty.

2335
01:34:10,971 --> 01:34:11,981
Gosh.

2336
01:34:11,981 --> 01:34:13,441
(The siblings follow the golden tickseed to the beach.)

2337
01:34:13,441 --> 01:34:14,511
Is this the right way?

2338
01:34:15,081 --> 01:34:16,751
- Gosh.
- There are butterflies.

2339
01:34:17,111 --> 01:34:18,181
These flowers are so pretty.

2340
01:34:18,181 --> 01:34:19,251
(Butterflies gather around Yoon Seo, thinking she's a flower.)

2341
01:34:19,251 --> 01:34:20,281
Gosh. It's so pretty.

2342
01:34:20,281 --> 01:34:22,351
The sand is so warm.

2343
01:34:22,351 --> 01:34:24,621
It feels nice. I'm going to walk barefoot.

2344
01:34:24,621 --> 01:34:26,321
(She takes off her shoes as the sand is fine and soft.)

2345
01:34:27,121 --> 01:34:29,031
- Gosh. This place is so romantic.
- It's pretty.

2346
01:34:29,031 --> 01:34:30,991
The beach is best in summer.

2347
01:34:31,561 --> 01:34:32,631
Gosh. I love it.

2348
01:34:33,501 --> 01:34:36,901
It feels like the beach in European films...

2349
01:34:37,301 --> 01:34:39,501
where a family visits for a vacation.

2350
01:34:40,101 --> 01:34:41,101
Exactly.

2351
01:34:41,371 --> 01:34:42,611
The colour is so pretty.

2352
01:34:43,771 --> 01:34:45,781
- Gosh. The sky is beautiful too.
- I love it.

2353
01:34:46,281 --> 01:34:48,411
(They love it.)

2354
01:34:48,781 --> 01:34:50,081
Should we dip our feet in the water?

2355
01:34:50,951 --> 01:34:51,981
Should we?

2356
01:34:52,151 --> 01:34:54,551
We need to dip our feet in the water while we're here.

2357
01:34:54,551 --> 01:34:56,391
(Let's deep our feet in the water as we've come to the beach.)

2358
01:34:57,251 --> 01:34:59,891
- Why are there no people?
- Yes. It's empty.

2359
01:35:00,121 --> 01:35:01,221
It's beautiful.

2360
01:35:01,861 --> 01:35:03,661
- The water comes up this far.
- Yes.

2361
01:35:05,101 --> 01:35:08,301
(Jung Ah walks across the white sand toward the sea.)

2362
01:35:08,301 --> 01:35:09,631
It's cold.

2363
01:35:10,631 --> 01:35:12,601
How's the water? Is it cold or not?

2364
01:35:12,601 --> 01:35:14,271
- It's very cold.
- She said it's very cold.

2365
01:35:15,571 --> 01:35:17,471
(A picturesque solo shot)

2366
01:35:17,471 --> 01:35:19,241
You look pretty, Jung Ah.

2367
01:35:19,841 --> 01:35:21,681
- Yes?
- You look pretty. Run for me.

2368
01:35:22,381 --> 01:35:23,481
- Run?
- Yes.

2369
01:35:23,711 --> 01:35:24,711
(Dashing)

2370
01:35:24,711 --> 01:35:26,951
No, Jung Ah. Not like that.

2371
01:35:27,421 --> 01:35:28,851
(When she is told to run,)

2372
01:35:28,851 --> 01:35:31,821
(she sprints at full speed.)

2373
01:35:32,161 --> 01:35:34,461
- Jung Ah!
- Jung Ah, jump.

2374
01:35:34,461 --> 01:35:36,491
No, Jung Ah. Run prettily with some style.

2375
01:35:36,491 --> 01:35:37,661
No? Didn't you ask her to jump?

2376
01:35:38,191 --> 01:35:39,201
Do you want me to hop?

2377
01:35:39,301 --> 01:35:41,531
No. Just run while looking graceful.

2378
01:35:41,531 --> 01:35:42,571
(Running gracefully)

2379
01:35:42,771 --> 01:35:43,931
(Scratching)

2380
01:35:45,171 --> 01:35:46,401
("Jung Ah is not here.")

2381
01:35:46,401 --> 01:35:47,671
(Running in a dorky way)

2382
01:35:48,641 --> 01:35:49,641
Jung Ah.

2383
01:35:49,641 --> 01:35:51,211
(She can't believe her.)

2384
01:35:52,141 --> 01:35:53,711
You can pull off slapstick now.

2385
01:35:55,481 --> 01:35:56,551
(Just hurry and come.)

2386
01:35:56,551 --> 01:35:57,611
It's hilarious.

2387
01:35:58,681 --> 01:36:00,221
How can she be so funny just by running?

2388
01:36:00,221 --> 01:36:02,221
(Following Jung Ah, they walk across the sandy beach.)

2389
01:36:02,221 --> 01:36:04,651
(Running)

2390
01:36:04,851 --> 01:36:07,021
- Isn't it cold? Are you okay?
- I'm good.

2391
01:36:07,021 --> 01:36:08,861
(The eldest is worried as the sea breeze is still cold.)

2392
01:36:10,331 --> 01:36:12,861
- Gosh. This place...
- It's so vast.

2393
01:36:12,861 --> 01:36:14,701
It feels too precious to walk over it.

2394
01:36:15,371 --> 01:36:16,671
It's like walking on the first snow.

2395
01:36:17,271 --> 01:36:20,241
How can it be this pretty? It's so clean.

2396
01:36:20,841 --> 01:36:22,371
Gosh. This is like...

2397
01:36:22,611 --> 01:36:25,211
- the beach in an Italian film.
- It's beautiful.

2398
01:36:25,681 --> 01:36:26,711
The beach I've never been to.

2399
01:36:26,711 --> 01:36:27,741
(Up close, it looks like the beach in an Italian film.)

2400
01:36:28,341 --> 01:36:30,351
- Gosh. I love it.
- Do you like it?

2401
01:36:30,351 --> 01:36:31,881
(It feels even better...)

2402
01:36:32,421 --> 01:36:36,491
(because they're here together at this beautiful place.)

2403
01:36:36,591 --> 01:36:38,991
- Gosh. They look fabulous.
- "How have you been?"

2404
01:36:38,991 --> 01:36:40,421
The two are looking great.

2405
01:36:40,921 --> 01:36:42,431
Don't they look like a couple...

2406
01:36:42,431 --> 01:36:43,961
- who have come to break up?
- A breakup trip?

2407
01:36:43,961 --> 01:36:44,961
- A breakup trip.
- A breakup trip.

2408
01:36:45,231 --> 01:36:46,231
Why do they break up?

2409
01:36:46,431 --> 01:36:48,361
It feels that way because of the colours.

2410
01:36:48,701 --> 01:36:49,771
(Amazed)

2411
01:36:50,131 --> 01:36:52,571
- The guy doesn't want to break up.
- I see.

2412
01:36:52,571 --> 01:36:53,571
But he has to.

2413
01:36:53,571 --> 01:36:56,471
- Right. He trudges along behind.
- Yes.

2414
01:36:58,211 --> 01:36:59,741
- And the view...
- It's so pretty.

2415
01:36:59,741 --> 01:37:00,781
Yes, it's so pretty.

2416
01:37:00,781 --> 01:37:01,911
(Do we really have to end it?)

2417
01:37:02,681 --> 01:37:04,411
Doesn't this place have a soulful vibe?

2418
01:37:04,951 --> 01:37:06,321
It's a bit...

2419
01:37:07,281 --> 01:37:08,591
It's a bit gloomy.

2420
01:37:08,991 --> 01:37:10,721
Right. I'm wearing sunglasses.

2421
01:37:11,451 --> 01:37:13,121
I wondered why it was so dark.

2422
01:37:14,021 --> 01:37:15,661
Why? What is it this time?

2423
01:37:15,661 --> 01:37:16,661
(What is going on again?)

2424
01:37:17,061 --> 01:37:20,101
- Hold on.
- I thought it felt gloomy...

2425
01:37:20,201 --> 01:37:21,361
for some reason.

2426
01:37:21,661 --> 01:37:23,801
These were why. And I thought,

2427
01:37:24,171 --> 01:37:25,941
(The sea is blue and so clear.)

2428
01:37:26,571 --> 01:37:29,071
(But for Sun Young, it was hazy and muted.)

2429
01:37:29,311 --> 01:37:31,571
"Gosh. This sea is so gloomy."

2430
01:37:31,571 --> 01:37:32,581
It was because of these.

2431
01:37:32,781 --> 01:37:35,381
- Let me try them on to see it.
- That was why I said...

2432
01:37:35,381 --> 01:37:37,751
the sea is gloomy like the one in an Italian film.

2433
01:37:37,751 --> 01:37:39,281
- Yes, Sun Young.
- That was it.

2434
01:37:39,281 --> 01:37:40,821
It feels like a non-digital film.

2435
01:37:40,821 --> 01:37:43,591
- Yes. Exactly.
- They mute the colours.

2436
01:37:43,591 --> 01:37:46,321
- They have a yellow filter.
- I can't believe myself.

2437
01:37:46,321 --> 01:37:47,561
(It looks like an old movie.)

2438
01:37:47,861 --> 01:37:50,991
- Everyone, I was wrong. It's...
- Sun Young.

2439
01:37:50,991 --> 01:37:52,031
(Embarrassed)

2440
01:37:52,331 --> 01:37:54,631
It's a clear, beautiful sea.

2441
01:37:54,631 --> 01:37:57,201
For goodness' sake. I thought they were breaking up.

2442
01:37:58,031 --> 01:37:59,571
I don't need them.

2443
01:38:01,141 --> 01:38:04,211
(You Seok dips his feet in the water.)

2444
01:38:04,211 --> 01:38:05,481
The water is cold, indeed.

2445
01:38:07,281 --> 01:38:10,811
(Yoon Seo dips her feet like You Seok.)

2446
01:38:11,611 --> 01:38:13,821
- It's nice and cold, Jung Ah.
- The water is cold.

2447
01:38:13,821 --> 01:38:14,821
(She walks right in while saying it's cold.)

2448
01:38:14,821 --> 01:38:15,851
It feels nice.

2449
01:38:16,291 --> 01:38:17,321
Gosh. We're at the sea!

2450
01:38:17,321 --> 01:38:19,491
(We need to enjoy the sea even though the water is cold.)

2451
01:38:20,091 --> 01:38:22,691
(At the beach, you have to play in the water.)

2452
01:38:23,331 --> 01:38:26,301
(Attacking Yoon Seo right away)

2453
01:38:27,501 --> 01:38:30,901
(She never goes easy on him just because he's older.)

2454
01:38:32,441 --> 01:38:35,271
(She grabs a floating piece of seaweed...)

2455
01:38:37,341 --> 01:38:38,411
(and surprises You Seok.)

2456
01:38:38,411 --> 01:38:39,411
You scared me.

2457
01:38:39,411 --> 01:38:41,041
(Laughing)

2458
01:38:41,481 --> 01:38:44,011
- Let's jump on 3.
- We'll jump on 3.

2459
01:38:44,251 --> 01:38:45,681
Jung Ah, we'll jump on three.

2460
01:38:45,681 --> 01:38:47,281
(These two are like our parents.)

2461
01:38:47,981 --> 01:38:50,591
- One, two, three.
- No!

2462
01:38:51,651 --> 01:38:52,791
(At the beach in Taean)

2463
01:38:52,791 --> 01:38:55,061
- Gosh. It's so pretty.
- Great.

2464
01:38:55,291 --> 01:38:56,731
Look at them.

2465
01:38:58,231 --> 01:38:59,701
Gosh. Fresh off the Sea.

2466
01:38:59,701 --> 01:39:01,761
(Leaving their mark on the beach before they leave)

2467
01:39:02,601 --> 01:39:04,301
- The letter suddenly got bigger.
- I know.

2468
01:39:04,831 --> 01:39:05,841
The first letter was too small.

2469
01:39:05,841 --> 01:39:07,571
(You Seok writes "Fresh.")

2470
01:39:08,441 --> 01:39:14,341
(And Yoon Seo writes "Off the Sea" below it.)

2471
01:39:15,041 --> 01:39:17,481
- Where should I put this?
- Between these letters.

2472
01:39:17,481 --> 01:39:20,621
(And the local specialties they can't leave out)

2473
01:39:21,381 --> 01:39:24,391
(We were here in Taean. Fresh off the Sea.)

2474
01:39:25,961 --> 01:39:28,161
- Bye.
- Bye.

2475
01:39:28,161 --> 01:39:29,591
(The siblings made new memories in Taean.)

2476
01:39:35,241 --> 01:39:36,301
(The siblings' third story, Hadong)

2477
01:39:36,941 --> 01:39:38,811
(Hiding beneath the winding Seomjin River...)

2478
01:39:38,811 --> 01:39:40,671
(are countless treasures.)

2479
01:39:40,941 --> 01:39:43,441
(Catch the marsh clams!)

2480
01:39:43,741 --> 01:39:46,681
(Welcome. Isn't it your first time working in the river?)

2481
01:39:47,011 --> 01:39:48,651
(But it's harder...)

2482
01:39:48,651 --> 01:39:50,251
(than they expected.)

2483
01:39:50,351 --> 01:39:52,721
(They work with a 15-kg pet georaengi.)

2484
01:39:52,921 --> 01:39:56,221
(The most gruelling labour)

2485
01:39:56,591 --> 01:40:00,861
(It’s almost a form of penance.)

2486
01:40:01,061 --> 01:40:02,961
(Suddenly,)

2487
01:40:02,961 --> 01:40:05,401
(the water gets deeper.)

2488
01:40:05,631 --> 01:40:08,301
(What will happen to the siblings in the Seomjin River?)

2489
01:40:08,571 --> 01:40:10,101
(And an insane menu lineup is on standby!)

2490
01:40:10,341 --> 01:40:12,741
(Made with freshly caught marsh clams)

2491
01:40:13,041 --> 01:40:17,641
(is the new type of clam chowder with marsh clams.)

2492
01:40:17,981 --> 01:40:19,781
(And Chef Yum's first kkakdugi in large quantity)

2493
01:40:20,081 --> 01:40:22,681
(You Seok is the head chef this time.)

2494
01:40:23,181 --> 01:40:26,651
(Crispy pork cutlet made by Chef Kang)

2495
01:40:26,921 --> 01:40:29,721
(The siblings' joyful dinner is coming soon!)
